{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MWnhgQ2EMmTfjG21S78rrX","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\",\"sha256\":\"d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\"},\"id\":\"claude-review-candidate-task\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a6d741a0b2f59eaa5f1a6919de5fc2fe6e164a734240de86a4301bbd8678ac86]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual claude Reviewer: candidate\\n\\nRoot selects the frozen claim in SELECTION.json. Read-only assessment; no source/candidate edits, repair, package installation, Git, model/subagent call or acceptance. Public a_c CLI writes only its own protected evidence. Bash/Read may inspect permitted sources and perform bounded in-memory/read-only probes. Do not write request files: use call --request - with an in-memory JSON envelope.\\n\\nAcquire your actual retained expectation through evidence.read and identify continuity from the prior source-only activation. Reacquire deciding sources as needed. Call review.prepare phase=candidate with this exact claim/candidate, selected proof sources, expectations=the bound prior ArtifactRef and expectation_body=null. Evaluate the real candidate and factual evidence against your source-derived expectations. Trace ordinary paths and material falsifiers, not counts. Return separate conclusions for every selected component. Record any missing scope, independence issue, tool refusal or changed expectation.\\n\\nThe governing source route is SELECTION.governing_sources. Candidate coordinates are metadata, not permission to read them before expectations. Shared requirements may govern tenant assessment, but common-WHAT candidate clauses cannot simultaneously be a pre-exposure governing source for their own review. If the selection has that overlap, return the exact missing basis instead of inventing source-first standing. Prior review expectations/verdicts are not your oracle. Disclose bootstrap/external exposure; no fresh context or family label certifies independence.\\n\\nUse the exact current native profile and tools.describe where needed. Native results.conjoin is unsupported. Source ownership and source-first law are the selected STDO3.0.1 release; no methodology duplication or stronger universal ceremony. Report S0-S4 findings with file:line, exact violated relation, reachable evidence and consequence; separate evidence from causal/repair inference. Record unperformed host qualification and efficiency claims as open, not pass/fail totals.\\n\\nThe public review.prepare request envelope is {\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"unique-id\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"review.prepare\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"phase\\\":\\\"expectation\\\" or \\\"candidate\\\",\\\"claim\\\":the CLAIM SourceRef,\\\"sources\\\":SELECTION.governing_sources,\\\"candidate\\\":SELECTION.candidate,\\\"proof\\\":[] for expectation or the selected proof SourceRefs,\\\"comparison\\\":null,\\\"expectations\\\":null for expectation or the bound ArtifactRef for candidate,\\\"expectation_body\\\":null for acquisition, then {\\\"text\\\":your actual source-derived expectations,\\\"source_inputs\\\":[actual prior acquisition ArtifactRefs]} when recording expectations}}. Source reads use arguments {\\\"source\\\":SourceRef,\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}. Evidence reads use {\\\"artifact\\\":ArtifactRef}. The first review.prepare response's evidence points to an OperationEvidence; evidence.read reveals envelope.payload.acquisitions, the actual source_inputs. Do not use OperationEvidence references where Acquisition references are required. Acquisition alone is not expectation recording: make the second expectation call with your own text.\\n\\nClosed return has exactly schema, id, frame, activation, subject, basis, actor, consumer, evaluations, not_performed, work_result, residuals, invalidators. schema=\\\"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\\\"; frame={id,revision}, activation={id,sha256}, subject={id,sha256}, basis={method_profile:{id,sha256},observations:[ArtifactRef]}, actor={id,family,authorship}, copied from actual Context. Each evaluation has exactly id, predicate (exact PREDICATES SourceRef), domain_outcome, core_value, evidence, residuals, invalidators. evidence contains actual SourceRefs/ArtifactRefs; residuals/invalidators are arrays. work_result=null. Use the return contract's evaluation id. A source-first expectation phase returns expectation-recording only, with the expectation artifact in evidence/domain_outcome; it does not assess the candidate.\\n\\nThis phase has 900 seconds under Root's explicit continuation budget; no retry. Inherited configured model/effort defaults remain unchanged. Final output is one original closed-return JSON object, no fences. Perform only the return contract's named evaluation and cite actual evidence; put unperformed evaluation IDs in not_performed. Candidate phase findings and per-component conclusions belong in domain_outcome. Never repair or replace the final original. Root owns continuation.\\n\\nThis is the candidate phase of the same actual Reviewer session 628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38. Your real source-first expectation is sha256:9ed61889acb0caaec032092f45fbfa888ea63b6ae74b0be56d1301990c67bc4a, produced by review.prepare in the completed source-only continuation. The original 300-second source-only attempt timed out; the 600-second continuation completed and recorded the artifact. Those facts are preserved, not reclassified as candidate review. Root selects a fresh 900-second candidate phase. Retain your disclosed bootstrap and tool-runtime exposure.\\n\\nUse that expectation unchanged. Do not repeat schema or expectation construction. Acquire candidate exactly once via the supplied review.prepare candidate request. Source payloads can be base64; decode only in memory, or use source.read encoding=utf8 for selected source text. No scratch-file/request-file writes. Use source acquisition evidence plus direct read-only source inspection as needed. The common and tool increment and Codex tenant are the exact 36-file population; Claude tenant is not in this claim. Keep actual paths and meaningful falsifiers ahead of counts. No Q01-Q12 host qualification is supplied by this static review. Return the original contract object before the 900-second bound, with any missing scope explicit.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\",\"size_bytes\":5787,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"claude-setup2/candidate/TASK.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"b7fbd5c6-3e63-4ce9-aca8-5e8c53451798","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:11:06.951Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\",\"sha256\":\"d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\"},\"id\":\"claude-review-candidate-task\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a6d741a0b2f59eaa5f1a6919de5fc2fe6e164a734240de86a4301bbd8678ac86]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Actual claude Reviewer: candidate\\n\\nRoot selects the frozen claim in SELECTION.json. Read-only assessment; no source/candidate edits, repair, package installation, Git, model/subagent call or acceptance. Public a_c CLI writes only its own protected evidence. Bash/Read may inspect permitted sources and perform bounded in-memory/read-only probes. Do not write request files: use call --request - with an in-memory JSON envelope.\\n\\nAcquire your actual retained expectation through evidence.read and identify continuity from the prior source-only activation. Reacquire deciding sources as needed. Call review.prepare phase=candidate with this exact claim/candidate, selected proof sources, expectations=the bound prior ArtifactRef and expectation_body=null. Evaluate the real candidate and factual evidence against your source-derived expectations. Trace ordinary paths and material falsifiers, not counts. Return separate conclusions for every selected component. Record any missing scope, independence issue, tool refusal or changed expectation.\\n\\nThe governing source route is SELECTION.governing_sources. Candidate coordinates are metadata, not permission to read them before expectations. Shared requirements may govern tenant assessment, but common-WHAT candidate clauses cannot simultaneously be a pre-exposure governing source for their own review. If the selection has that overlap, return the exact missing basis instead of inventing source-first standing. Prior review expectations/verdicts are not your oracle. Disclose bootstrap/external exposure; no fresh context or family label certifies independence.\\n\\nUse the exact current native profile and tools.describe where needed. Native results.conjoin is unsupported. Source ownership and source-first law are the selected STDO3.0.1 release; no methodology duplication or stronger universal ceremony. Report S0-S4 findings with file:line, exact violated relation, reachable evidence and consequence; separate evidence from causal/repair inference. Record unperformed host qualification and efficiency claims as open, not pass/fail totals.\\n\\nThe public review.prepare request envelope is {\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"unique-id\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"review.prepare\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"phase\\\":\\\"expectation\\\" or \\\"candidate\\\",\\\"claim\\\":the CLAIM SourceRef,\\\"sources\\\":SELECTION.governing_sources,\\\"candidate\\\":SELECTION.candidate,\\\"proof\\\":[] for expectation or the selected proof SourceRefs,\\\"comparison\\\":null,\\\"expectations\\\":null for expectation or the bound ArtifactRef for candidate,\\\"expectation_body\\\":null for acquisition, then {\\\"text\\\":your actual source-derived expectations,\\\"source_inputs\\\":[actual prior acquisition ArtifactRefs]} when recording expectations}}. Source reads use arguments {\\\"source\\\":SourceRef,\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}. Evidence reads use {\\\"artifact\\\":ArtifactRef}. The first review.prepare response's evidence points to an OperationEvidence; evidence.read reveals envelope.payload.acquisitions, the actual source_inputs. Do not use OperationEvidence references where Acquisition references are required. Acquisition alone is not expectation recording: make the second expectation call with your own text.\\n\\nClosed return has exactly schema, id, frame, activation, subject, basis, actor, consumer, evaluations, not_performed, work_result, residuals, invalidators. schema=\\\"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\\\"; frame={id,revision}, activation={id,sha256}, subject={id,sha256}, basis={method_profile:{id,sha256},observations:[ArtifactRef]}, actor={id,family,authorship}, copied from actual Context. Each evaluation has exactly id, predicate (exact PREDICATES SourceRef), domain_outcome, core_value, evidence, residuals, invalidators. evidence contains actual SourceRefs/ArtifactRefs; residuals/invalidators are arrays. work_result=null. Use the return contract's evaluation id. A source-first expectation phase returns expectation-recording only, with the expectation artifact in evidence/domain_outcome; it does not assess the candidate.\\n\\nThis phase has 900 seconds under Root's explicit continuation budget; no retry. Inherited configured model/effort defaults remain unchanged. Final output is one original closed-return JSON object, no fences. Perform only the return contract's named evaluation and cite actual evidence; put unperformed evaluation IDs in not_performed. Candidate phase findings and per-component conclusions belong in domain_outcome. Never repair or replace the final original. Root owns continuation.\\n\\nThis is the candidate phase of the same actual Reviewer session 628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38. Your real source-first expectation is sha256:9ed61889acb0caaec032092f45fbfa888ea63b6ae74b0be56d1301990c67bc4a, produced by review.prepare in the completed source-only continuation. The original 300-second source-only attempt timed out; the 600-second continuation completed and recorded the artifact. Those facts are preserved, not reclassified as candidate review. Root selects a fresh 900-second candidate phase. Retain your disclosed bootstrap and tool-runtime exposure.\\n\\nUse that expectation unchanged. Do not repeat schema or expectation construction. Acquire candidate exactly once via the supplied review.prepare candidate request. Source payloads can be base64; decode only in memory, or use source.read encoding=utf8 for selected source text. No scratch-file/request-file writes. Use source acquisition evidence plus direct read-only source inspection as needed. The common and tool increment and Codex tenant are the exact 36-file population; Claude tenant is not in this claim. Keep actual paths and meaningful falsifiers ahead of counts. No Q01-Q12 host qualification is supplied by this static review. Return the original contract object before the 900-second bound, with any missing scope explicit.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\",\"size_bytes\":5787,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"claude-setup2/candidate/TASK.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"a71ae90521ac254c8bfe8277cdc7419cb781e9eb11c44aa81927f9f14141285d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MWnhgQ2EMmTfjG21S78rrX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
