{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNDxrCJetQoMgWk1uiMf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XJPrvGAZm48K3wi4bmrerj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","offset":2241,"limit":736},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7166,"cache_read_input_tokens":247181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7166},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"22506f38-6aec-4f0e-a773-e24094df6056","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:12:40.085Z","request_id":"req_011CgNDxqxAK1Who3PGXriGQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XJPrvGAZm48K3wi4bmrerj":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","offset":2241,"limit":736}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XJPrvGAZm48K3wi4bmrerj","type":"tool_result","content":"2241\t######## [14] product:.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md sel=None ########\n2242\t    1| # T-001 — Build STDO Skills with STDO 3.0.1 and current tools\n2243\t    2| \n2244\t    3| Status: active construction; common source is a candidate. Product acceptance,\n2245\t    4| publication and general benefit remain open.\n2246\t    5| \n2247\t    6| ## Owner instruction\n2248\t    7| \n2249\t    8| The owner first selected a separate root-level `stdo_skills/` Product, shared\n2250\t    9| requirements, and independent Codex and Claude skill build tenants tuned to their\n2251\t   10| hosts. The immediate concrete proposal named `stdo_skills.json`, common\n2252\t   11| `specification/` and `build_tenants/{codex,claude}/` with designs, skills and tests.\n2253\t   12| Jim then instructed:\n2254\t   13| \n2255\t   14| > yes the are decoupled, this is a test, eating our own dog food,\n2256\t   15| > 1. pin stdo 3.0.1 as the static released methodology against specification_method\n2257\t   16| > 2. as executive build out of stdo skills, use the current tooling to build the skills\n2258\t   17| \n2259\t   18| This binds the construction outcome and method selection. It does not accept\n2260\t   19| documents yet to be written or authorize remote publication or global deployment.\n2261\t   20| \n2262\t   21| ## Work basis and current admission interpretation\n2263\t   22| \n2264\t   23| The static methodology is `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n2265\t   24| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`;\n2266\t   25| native commit `fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9`.\n2267\t   26| The isolated source worktree is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills`,\n2268\t   27| branch `codex/stdo-skills`, initial repository base\n2269\t   28| `a2e56d8bd2882068c84e45b2423cecc246c62525`.\n2270\t   29| \n2271\t   30| Root's Writer activation selects the exact proposed construction and bounded\n2272\t   31| territory under the recorded owner instruction. Root explicitly directs the\n2273\t   32| initial Writer to consume that existing human authorization and create a\n2274\t   33| reviewable common candidate, without claiming a deterministic admission result.\n2275\t   34| This is the bounded construction interpretation used here. It is not a fabricated\n2276\t   35| human override of a later unseen contract, a tool-issued admission, an accepted\n2277\t   36| Project frame basis or proof of completed STDO application.\n2278\t   37| \n2279\t   38| ACTIVATION §1 Admission requires exact-contract admission evidence for governed\n2280\t   39| execution. Integration of that requirement with subsequent real delegated\n2281\t   40| operation contracts is an open tool/application obligation, E03, and must be\n2282\t   41| resolved before claiming the native supported lifecycle path. Recording a drafted\n2283\t   42| contract or this ticket cannot supply that evidence. Any review disagreement\n2284\t   43| about the initial construction interpretation remains attached to these effects;\n2285\t   44| it cannot be erased by a later successful test.\n2286\t   45| \n2287\t   46| ## Outcome and decision scope\n2288\t   47| \n2289\t   48| Deliver independently designed and usable Codex/Claude skill packages against\n2290\t   49| common requirements, static methodology and actual supported tools. Root is the\n2291\t   50| Executive: it keeps the outcome/frontier, selects bounded requirements/design\n2292\t   51| candidates for construction, allocates Writer operations, assesses closed returns\n2293\t   52| and orders supported repairs. Product acceptance/release and changed Product\n2294\t   53| meaning remain with Jim. Root does not mutate while occupying Executive.\n2295\t   54| \n2296\t   55| Common documents and the frame configuration remain candidates until an exact\n2297\t   56| Root construction disposition is recorded. That disposition supplies only the\n2298\t   57| decisions covered by Root's grant; it is not owner acceptance or a substitute\n2299\t   58| for required execution admission.\n2300\t   59| \n2301\t   60| ## Territory and effects\n2302\t   61| \n2303\t   62| - Bootstrap Writer: isolated worktree creation, exact static installation,\n2304\t   63|   `stdo_skills.json` and bootstrap evidence; no adoption into existing Products.\n2305\t   64| - Common Writer: this ticket, Product README/AGENTS/CLAUDE, `specification/`,\n2306\t   65|   `build_tenants/README.md` and `.ai-workspace/work/T001/common/` only.\n2307\t   66| - Tenant Writers: their separately bound `build_tenants/codex/` or `claude/`\n2308\t   67|   territory and named evidence surfaces, after Root activation.\n2309\t   68| - Qualification: disposable declared workspaces and exact retained evidence,\n2310\t   69|   with actual host/model/resource settings recorded before execution.\n2311\t   70| - a_c repairs: separately bounded owner territory and supported contract change;\n2312\t   71|   no tenant silently forks tool semantics. No modification of released STDO.\n2313\t   72| \n2314\t   73| Preserve unrelated worktrees and files. No commit, push, remote publication or\n2315\t   74| global skill configuration change follows from a common Writer or tenant grant.\n2316\t   75| Any later checkpoint/distribution operation needs its exact existing scope bound.\n2317\t   76| \n2318\t   77| ## Execution plan and ledger\n2319\t   78| \n2320\t   79| | Stage | Required result | Current standing |\n2321\t   80| |---|---|---|\n2322\t   81| | 1. Pin | Installed 3.0.1 integrity and definition binding | Bootstrap evidence retained; common Writer independently observed valid verification |\n2323\t   82| | 2. Common WHAT | Intent, Product, requirements, scenarios and frame proposal | Candidate delivered for Root disposition and review |\n2324\t   83| | 3. Tool binding | Per-operation 3.0.1 support or exact justified translation, including admission | Current-tool assessment in progress; RC9 lifecycle support does not establish this |\n2325\t   84| | 4. Tenant design/build | Independent Codex and Claude HOW with requirement trace and runnable packages | Pending respective bounded activations |\n2326\t   85| | 5. Actual use | Common Q01..12 outcomes and actual tool-path evidence on both hosts | Not performed by this common Writer |\n2327\t   86| | 6. Independent assessment | Exact candidates, source-derived oracle, findings and supported repairs | Pending |\n2328\t   87| | 7. Delivery disposition | Truthful supported claims, effects and residuals | Pending; no release selected |\n2329\t   88| \n2330\t   89| Use the smallest dependency-ready frontier. Common-source review and host-design\n2331\t   90| preparation may proceed while tool compatibility is resolved; operations that\n2332\t   91| depend on unsupported contracts remain withheld. No task is restarted merely\n2333\t   92| because another role is activated. A demonstrated counterexample determines the\n2334\t   93| affected re-entry and scope of repair.\n2335\t   94| \n2336\t   95| ## Proof and closure\n2337\t   96| \n2338\t   97| The durable result/evidence surface is `.ai-workspace/work/T001/`.\n2339\t   98| The common Writer's exact inventory, source/tool observations, structural checks\n2340\t   99| and return are under `common/`. Bootstrap retains actual installer evidence under\n2341\t  100| `bootstrap/`. Later activations append their own exact-source results and costs.\n2342\t  101| \n2343\t  102| The [common scenarios](../../../specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md) define\n2344\t  103| observable predicates, not expected wording. The initial delivery claim requires\n2345\t  104| both usable tenant implementations, supported declared tool paths, mandatory\n2346\t  105| finite scenario evidence and independent assessment with supported repairs.\n2347\t  106| Missing results, changed bases, unknown effects or unresolved required conditions\n2348\t  107| withhold affected closure. Metadata validation and test totals alone cannot close\n2349\t  108| the Product outcome. Root reports partial results honestly if a resource or\n2350\t  109| authority boundary stops work.\n2351\t  110| \n2352\t  111| ## Re-entry and stop conditions\n2353\t  112| \n2354\t  113| Re-enter the relevant owner for missing or changed Product meaning, unsupported\n2355\t  114| tool semantics, insufficient context, actual host capability mismatch, invalid\n2356\t  115| source custody, or a counterexample to required behavior. Reconcile uncertain\n2357\t  116| effects before retry. Retain open obligations and prior attempts. Stop the\n2358\t  117| dependent operation for missing authority, an unresolved hard boundary, exhausted\n2359\t  118| declared envelope or an unsupported contract. Continue unrelated authorized work\n2360\t  119| where its basis remains sufficient.\n2361\t  120| \n2362\t  121| No failure or review result changes the static method pin. A proposed new method\n2363\t  122| adoption, Product scope change or publication returns to Jim with its concrete\n2364\t  123| consequences. Routine implementation choices and supported repairs stay within\n2365\t  124| the selected construction mandate.\n2366\t  125| \n2367\t\n2368\t######## [15] product:AGENTS.md sel=None ########\n2369\t    1| # STDO Skills bootstrap\n2370\t    2| \n2371\t    3| Select `stdo_skills.json`, verify its exact installed basis with `stdo status\n2372\t    4| --definition stdo_skills.json --verify`, and read the declared bootstrap and\n2373\t    5| deciding owner sections from that installation. The operative cut is STDO\n2374\t    6| v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n2375\t    7| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2376\t    8| Do not adopt a newer cut from the discovery selector implicitly.\n2377\t    9| \n2378\t   10| Read README, Intent, Product, Goals, requirements and the current frame-basis\n2379\t   11| disposition. Common WHAT belongs in `specification/`. Codex and Claude are\n2380\t   12| independent HOW tenants, each with its own design and skills. Shared requirements\n2381\t   13| do not require identical prompts, decomposition or host machinery.\n2382\t   14| \n2383\t   15| The initial common documents are candidates for Executive construction\n2384\t   16| disposition. Their presence and the Product Definition locator are not evidence\n2385\t   17| of acceptance. T-001 records the owner's concrete construction instruction and\n2386\t   18| the current admission/tooling limitation.\n2387\t   19| \n2388\t   20| Executive coordinates; it does not mutate. A separately bound Worker/Writer\n2389\t   21| performs exact named effects. Use bounded delegation for material context,\n2390\t   22| capability or independence boundaries. A sufficient small task may use direct\n2391\t   23| Writer entry without automatic tickets or independent review. Reviewers acquire\n2392\t   24| source-derived expectations and the exact candidate independently and return\n2393\t   25| findings; they do not implement repairs or decide promotion.\n2394\t   26| \n2395\t   27| Use the declared supported tool contracts and retain actual responses. Required\n2396\t   28| tool failure or an unsupported method binding withholds its dependent claim;\n2397\t   29| do not simulate a passing result or silently bypass the required path. Preserve\n2398\t   30| unrelated work and the frozen released methodology. Native tools and actor calls\n2399\t   31| are mechanisms, not new admission, acceptance or release authority.\n2400\t   32| \n2401\t\n2402\t######## [16] product:CLAUDE.md sel=None ########\n2403\t    1| # STDO Skills bootstrap\n2404\t    2| \n2405\t    3| Select `stdo_skills.json`, verify its exact installed basis with `stdo status\n2406\t    4| --definition stdo_skills.json --verify`, and read the declared bootstrap and\n2407\t    5| deciding owner sections from that installation. The operative cut is STDO\n2408\t    6| v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n2409\t    7| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2410\t    8| Do not adopt a newer cut from the discovery selector implicitly.\n2411\t    9| \n2412\t   10| Read README, Intent, Product, Goals, requirements and the current frame-basis\n2413\t   11| disposition. Common WHAT belongs in `specification/`. Codex and Claude are\n2414\t   12| independent HOW tenants, each with its own design and skills. Shared requirements\n2415\t   13| do not require identical prompts, decomposition or host machinery.\n2416\t   14| \n2417\t   15| The initial common documents are candidates for Executive construction\n2418\t   16| disposition. Their presence and the Product Definition locator are not evidence\n2419\t   17| of acceptance. T-001 records the owner's concrete construction instruction and\n2420\t   18| the current admission/tooling limitation.\n2421\t   19| \n2422\t   20| Executive coordinates; it does not mutate. A separately bound Worker/Writer\n2423\t   21| performs exact named effects. Use bounded delegation for material context,\n2424\t   22| capability or independence boundaries. A sufficient small task may use direct\n2425\t   23| Writer entry without automatic tickets or independent review. Reviewers acquire\n2426\t   24| source-derived expectations and the exact candidate independently and return\n2427\t   25| findings; they do not implement repairs or decide promotion.\n2428\t   26| \n2429\t   27| Use the declared supported tool contracts and retain actual responses. Required\n2430\t   28| tool failure or an unsupported method binding withholds its dependent claim;\n2431\t   29| do not simulate a passing result or silently bypass the required path. Preserve\n2432\t   30| unrelated work and the frozen released methodology. Native tools and actor calls\n2433\t   31| are mechanisms, not new admission, acceptance or release authority.\n2434\t   32| \n2435\t\n2436\t######## [17] product:README.md sel=None ########\n2437\t    1| # STDO Skills\n2438\t    2| \n2439\t    3| STDO Skills makes the selected STDO method usable in ordinary agent work through\n2440\t    4| tool-backed skills. One shared specification has two independent build tenants:\n2441\t    5| Codex and Claude. Each tenant may choose different skill boundaries, instructions,\n2442\t    6| context mechanisms and host integration while preserving the same requirements.\n2443\t    7| \n2444\t    8| This is a construction candidate. The current work is [T-001](.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\n2445\t    9| Read [Intent](specification/INTENT.md), [Product](specification/PRODUCT.md),\n2446\t   10| [Goals](specification/GOALS.md), [requirements](specification/requirements/README.md)\n2447\t   11| and the [frame basis](specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md).\n2448\t   12| \n2449\t   13| The static methodology is **STDO 3.0.1 RC1**, selected by\n2450\t   14| [stdo_skills.json](stdo_skills.json). Its manifest is\n2451\t   15| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2452\t   16| The discovery selector never substitutes for that operative basis.\n2453\t   17| \n2454\t   18| ```sh\n2455\t   19| stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify\n2456\t   20| ```\n2457\t   21| \n2458\t   22| STDO owns methodology; a_c owns computational support tools; this Product owns\n2459\t   23| the agent-facing application of those contracts. Their release and adoption\n2460\t   24| decisions remain separate. Existing installed STDO skills are donor material,\n2461\t   25| not the new tenants' accepted implementation.\n2462\t   26| \n2463\t   27| Current a_c lifecycle tooling has a Claude RC9 method binding. Its support for\n2464\t   28| 3.0.1 must be established per operation. An honest legacy mechanical acquisition\n2465\t   29| can supply source bytes; it does not establish 3.0.1 lifecycle admission,\n2466\t   30| conjunction or semantic qualification. See the\n2467\t   31| [tool-binding requirement](specification/requirements/README.md#sk-04-supported-tool-use).\n2468\t   32| \n2469\t   33| The initial proof is a matched finite set of realistic tasks on both hosts,\n2470\t   34| including automatic discovery, explicit invocation, tool failures and recovery.\n2471\t   35| Passing metadata checks alone does not show that agents use the tooling.\n2472\t   36| \n2473\t\n2474\t######## [18] product:build_tenants/README.md sel=None ########\n2475\t    1| # Skill build tenants\n2476\t    2| \n2477\t    3| | Tenant | Target execution environment | Owned realization |\n2478\t    4| |---|---|---|\n2479\t    5| | `codex` | Declared Codex host/version and model/settings | Codex design, skill decomposition, prompts, supporting resources, installation and qualification |\n2480\t    6| | `claude` | Declared Claude host/version and model/settings | Claude design, skill decomposition, prompts, supporting resources, installation and qualification |\n2481\t    7| \n2482\t    8| Both implement [the same requirements](../specification/requirements/README.md)\n2483\t    9| under the Product's pinned STDO 3.0.1 basis. Each design must show its calculus\n2484\t   10| binding from requirements to operations and its execution binding to the actual\n2485\t   11| host, including material effects, failure behavior and resource assumptions.\n2486\t   12| \n2487\t   13| Tenant differences require a supported host or behavioral reason. Shared contract\n2488\t   14| meaning is not copied and independently changed in prompt text. Skill names,\n2489\t   15| counts and wording may differ; qualification compares outcomes and required paths.\n2490\t   16| Existing STDO plugin skills may be selected as exact donors, then revised as the\n2491\t   17| requirements demand. No donor inherits acceptance into this Product.\n2492\t   18| \n2493\t   19| The public surface for each tenant includes its install/discovery route, explicit\n2494\t   20| invocation, ordinary task behavior, supported tools and removal/update behavior.\n2495\t   21| Keep host mechanics in tenant HOW and tool algorithms with their existing owner.\n2496\t   22| Do not invent a shared skill runtime to make the directories symmetrical.\n2497\t   23| \n2498\t   24| Construction remains isolated to the tenant's granted territory. Shared WHAT\n2499\t   25| changes return to Root. A review identifies its exact candidate and exposure;\n2500\t   26| one tenant's success supplies no qualification for the other host.\n2501\t   27| \n2502\t\n2503\t######## [19] product:specification/GOALS.md sel=None ########\n2504\t    1| # Goals\n2505\t    2| \n2506\t    3| ## Current selection\n2507\t    4| \n2508\t    5| [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md) constructs the new\n2509\t    6| STDO Skills Product using static released STDO 3.0.1 RC1 and current tooling.\n2510\t    7| The common WHAT is shared; Codex and Claude receive independently designed and\n2511\t    8| tuned build tenants. This is the initial practical test of the method on its own\n2512\t    9| agent tooling.\n2513\t   10| \n2514\t   11| Current common documents are candidates awaiting Root's exact construction\n2515\t   12| disposition. Bootstrap installed-basis verification is evidence about the basis,\n2516\t   13| not proof of the skills. Tool compatibility assessment is in progress.\n2517\t   14| \n2518\t   15| ## Delivery outcomes\n2519\t   16| \n2520\t   17| 1. Verify the immutable method pin and preserve it throughout construction.\n2521\t   18| 2. Establish common capabilities, discriminators, frame basis and work authority.\n2522\t   19| 3. Resolve the tool contracts required by the selected lifecycle paths.\n2523\t   20| 4. Construct independent Codex and Claude designs and working skill packages.\n2524\t   21| 5. Exercise matched finite scenarios on actual hosts and inspect actual tool calls.\n2525\t   22| 6. Obtain independent assessment, repair supported defects and present a bounded\n2526\t   23|    delivery result with all remaining limitations.\n2527\t   24| \n2528\t   25| The [T-001 ledger](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md#execution-plan-and-ledger)\n2529\t   26| owns detailed progress. Publication, fleet deployment, global default changes and\n2530\t   27| general efficiency claims are outside the initial delivery result.\n2531\t   28| \n2532\t\n2533\t######## [20] product:specification/INTENT.md sel=None ########\n2534\t    1| # Intent\n2535\t    2| \n2536\t    3| Make STDO usable through skills that help agents choose and perform the right\n2537\t    4| work with the available computational tools. Reduce repeated ad hoc context\n2538\t    5| construction, omitted checks and recovery mistakes while preserving the owner's\n2539\t    6| outcome and the methodology's distinctions.\n2540\t    7| \n2541\t    8| Build one common Product with independently tuned Codex and Claude realizations.\n2542\t    9| Keep the released STDO 3.0.1 methodology static during this experiment. Use the\n2543\t   10| method and current tools to build the skills, exposing real integration gaps as\n2544\t   11| evidence rather than explaining them away.\n2545\t   12| \n2546\t   13| Demonstrate actual tool use and useful outcomes on declared tasks before claiming\n2547\t   14| effective operation. Efficiency improvement and reliable automatic selection are\n2548\t   15| empirical claims to measure, not consequences of packaging instructions as skills.\n2549\t   16| \n2550\t\n2551\t######## [21] product:specification/PRODUCT.md sel=None ########\n2552\t    1| # STDO Skills\n2553\t    2| \n2554\t    3| Status: common construction candidate under T-001; not Product acceptance or release.\n2555\t    4| \n2556\t    5| ## Product boundary\n2557\t    6| \n2558\t    7| Product identity: `urn:stdo:product-definition:stdo-skills`.\n2559\t    8| Bounded context: `urn:stdo-skills:bounded-context:agent-method-application`.\n2560\t    9| \n2561\t   10| The Product supplies skills for F_P agents applying an exactly selected STDO\n2562\t   11| methodology to software-development work. It connects recognizable user tasks\n2563\t   12| to the deciding source, appropriate context, supported tool operations and\n2564\t   13| observable returns. It owns requirements for this user-facing capability and\n2565\t   14| evidence that each tenant realizes it.\n2566\t   15| \n2567\t   16| STDO owns the method. a_c and other declared Development Products own their tool\n2568\t   17| contracts and computational implementations. A skill preserves and applies those\n2569\t   18| contracts; it does not create another lifecycle, state store or source of\n2570\t   19| assessment, admission, acceptance or publication authority.\n2571\t   20| \n2572\t   21| ## Selected methodology\n2573\t   22| \n2574\t   23| The complete static builder and initial supported methodology is\n2575\t   24| `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n2576\t   25| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2577\t   26| Native commit: `fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9`;\n2578\t   27| package: `specification_methodology/v3`.\n2579\t   28| The [Product Definition](../stdo_skills.json) owns the operative locator.\n2580\t   29| The mutable `3.0.1` discovery channel is not an adoption instruction.\n2581\t   30| \n2582\t   31| The release remains static while this Product's requirements, designs and skills\n2583\t   32| are developed. A later method adoption requires an explicit compatibility\n2584\t   33| decision and affected qualification; an implementation defect does not authorize\n2585\t   34| editing the selected methodology.\n2586\t   35| \n2587\t   36| ## Users and capability\n2588\t   37| \n2589\t   38| The user works in a governed workspace using Codex or Claude. Skills support:\n2590\t   39| \n2591\t   40| - setup and exact Product/method selection;\n2592\t   41| - intake and re-entry at the changed requirement, design or realization owner;\n2593\t   42| - context acquisition and bounded frame construction;\n2594\t   43| - authorized direct work or Executive-directed delegation;\n2595\t   44| - source-first independent review where required;\n2596\t   45| - continuation, recovery, currentness and truthful status;\n2597\t   46| - release preparation and separately authorized release operations.\n2598\t   47| \n2599\t   48| The shared requirements state outcomes and discriminators. They do not prescribe\n2600\t   49| skill count, names, prompt identity, invocation syntax or host-specific mechanism.\n2601\t   50| Each tenant owns its computational and execution binding, including instructions,\n2602\t   51| supporting references, tool integration, installation and tuning.\n2603\t   52| \n2604\t   53| ## Tool relationship\n2605\t   54| \n2606\t   55| The current `stdo` manager can verify and resolve the exact installation. Existing\n2607\t   56| a_c mechanics are available through an explicitly selected implementation and\n2608\t   57| method binding. The current legacy lifecycle profile is not renamed to 3.0.1.\n2609\t   58| Each operation used for a 3.0.1 claim needs established compatibility or a declared\n2610\t   59| supported translation. Reading opaque source bytes under an honestly identified\n2611\t   60| legacy acquisition contract makes only that acquisition claim.\n2612\t   61| \n2613\t   62| Tool harmonisation remains owned by a_c. This Product may identify required\n2614\t   63| contracts, report defects and consume a supported increment; it does not fork\n2615\t   64| tool semantics into each tenant. A skill's direct use of host facilities must\n2616\t   65| be declared in its design, preserve the selected operation contract and be\n2617\t   66| qualified on that actual path. It cannot substitute for a required tool result.\n2618\t   67| \n2619\t   68| F_D classification follows the selected calculus's totality and dependency\n2620\t   69| requirements. An F_D constructor gains no assessment or admission authority from\n2621\t   70| that classification; invoking an F_P actor does not make its semantic answer\n2622\t   71| deterministic. The deciding owners are in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\n2623\t   72| \n2624\t   73| ## Independent tenants and releases\n2625\t   74| \n2626\t   75| `build_tenants/codex/` and `build_tenants/claude/` independently realize the common\n2627\t   76| WHAT. Evidence and supported-host claims are tenant-specific. Both use the same\n2628\t   77| task semantics and acceptance predicates, while host realization and tuning may\n2629\t   78| differ materially. Common machinery is reused where its contract fits; retained\n2630\t   79| variants need a concrete supported difference.\n2631\t   80| \n2632\t   81| This Product is a peer at the monorepo root. It has its own lifecycle and release\n2633\t   82| identity and is not automatically a member of an existing STDO release cohort.\n2634\t   83| The present work constructs candidates and performs bounded qualification; it\n2635\t   84| does not publish a release or install skills into unrelated user environments.\n2636\t   85| \n2637\t   86| ## Construction authority\n2638\t   87| \n2639\t   88| Jim owns Product scope, common meaning, acceptance and release. His recorded\n2640\t   89| [T-001 instruction](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md#owner-instruction)\n2641\t   90| selects this Product, its two tenants, static method and Executive-directed\n2642\t   91| construction. Root is the bounded Executive for that work and can select\n2643\t   92| requirements/design candidates for construction, allocate exact Writer effects,\n2644\t   93| evaluate returns, request supported repairs and retain residuals within that\n2645\t   94| outcome. It cannot silently broaden Product meaning or claim owner acceptance.\n2646\t   95| \n2647\t   96| The current [frame basis](REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md) is proposed for this\n2648\t   97| construction. Its disposition must be recorded against exact candidate bytes.\n2649\t   98| The owner's work authorization, a drafted execution contract, deterministic\n2650\t   99| admission and acceptance remain distinct. T-001 records the initial construction\n2651\t  100| interpretation and the unresolved integration of later admission contracts.\n2652\t  101| \n2653\t  102| ## Acceptance boundary\n2654\t  103| \n2655\t  104| Initial delivery requires a coherent common specification, both realized tenant\n2656\t  105| designs, usable host installation paths, supported tool bindings, and independent\n2657\t  106| assessment of the [finite scenario evidence](requirements/SCENARIOS.md).\n2658\t  107| Missing or failed mandatory evidence withholds the corresponding supported claim.\n2659\t  108| It cannot be hidden by a suite total or by the other tenant succeeding.\n2660\t  109| \n2661\t  110| Repeated use may establish broader reliability and benefit. This first experiment\n2662\t  111| supports only the cases, hosts, settings, tool versions and outcomes actually\n2663\t  112| observed. Product acceptance and release remain owner decisions on that evidence.\n2664\t  113| \n2665\t\n2666\t######## [22] product:specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md sel=None ########\n2667\t    1| # Project reference-frame basis\n2668\t    2| \n2669\t    3| Identity: `urn:stdo-skills:frame-basis:initial:1`.\n2670\t    4| Status: proposed construction configuration; Root disposition over its exact\n2671\t    5| bytes is pending. The Product Definition points here as its intended basis;\n2672\t    6| that pointer does not establish acceptance.\n2673\t    7| \n2674\t    8| ## Method, outcome and authority\n2675\t    9| \n2676\t   10| The complete method is STDO v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n2677\t   11| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2678\t   12| Read the exact installed REFERENCE_FRAME and ACTIVATION owners. This configuration\n2679\t   13| applies the Executive/Worker/Reviewer relations of EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10,\n2680\t   14| 12 and 16 to the owner's selected dogfood construction, while retaining the\n2681\t   15| sufficient direct Writer branch. It makes no claim of completed profile\n2682\t   16| qualification or automatic applicability of every available specialist frame.\n2683\t   17| \n2684\t   18| The governed mutable source is this `stdo_skills/` Product. The outcome is two\n2685\t   19| usable skill tenants satisfying the common requirements and assessed on the\n2686\t   20| finite declared tasks. Jim owns Product acceptance and release. Root's bounded\n2687\t   21| construction decisions and exact user instruction are in [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\n2688\t   22| An actor label supplies no effect grant or admission. The initial construction\n2689\t   23| interpretation and subsequent admission obligation remain explicit there.\n2690\t   24| \n2691\t   25| ## Frames and coordinates\n2692\t   26| \n2693\t   27| | Frame | Evaluation and material attention | Authority, evidence and return |\n2694\t   28| |---|---|---|\n2695\t   29| | Executive `skills.executive/1` | Exact Product outcome, dependency-ready frontier, current candidate identities, closed returns, tool compatibility and remaining claims | Select only authorized bounded actions; no mutation in this frame; consumes source-bound returns and records decisions through a granted Writer |\n2696\t   30| | Worker `skills.worker/1` | Exact requirement/design, affected producers/consumers, selected host/tool contracts, operation territory and proof predicates | Construct only within grant; self-review and return exact candidate, performed/unperformed evaluations, effects, residuals and invalidators to Executive |\n2697\t   31| | Reviewer `skills.reviewer/1` | Source-derived expected behavior, exact frozen candidate and actual-path evidence, exposure history and test semantics | Independent assessment, not repair or promotion; return findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty to Executive |\n2698\t   32| | Direct Writer `skills.direct-writer/1` | One sufficient local outcome, existing basis and effect grant, current preimage and focused proof | No coordination or independent review added solely from task existence; admission and exact territory still required; return to declared consumer |\n2699\t   33| \n2700\t   34| Each activation names frame/revision, exact evaluation/result algebra, subject and\n2701\t   35| basis, material invariants, authorities, evidence/tools, capability/context\n2702\t   36| envelope, exclusions, dependencies, consumer and stop/re-entry conditions, as\n2703\t   37| REFERENCE_FRAME §11 requires. File identities use content hashes or exact commits;\n2704\t   38| host/model settings and tool/profile versions are material coordinates. Results\n2705\t   39| use ACTIVATION's work/result refinements with named predicates, not an invented\n2706\t   40| local pass algebra.\n2707\t   41| \n2708\t   42| No actor receives the entire repository merely because it is available. The\n2709\t   43| Executive selects the deciding frontier. Workers acquire the causal cone needed\n2710\t   44| for their own change; Reviewers acquire sources independently. Measured task\n2711\t   45| context, actor capability and remaining unknowns accompany each activation.\n2712\t   46| \n2713\t   47| ## Known evaluation inventory and coverage\n2714\t   48| \n2715\t   49| | Evaluation | Source and dependency | Current disposition |\n2716\t   50| |---|---|---|\n2717\t   51| | E01 Exact static method and definition | Product selection; manager verification | Bootstrap evidence available; definition completion remains tied to common disposition |\n2718\t   52| | E02 Common outcome and requirement adequacy | Intent, Product, SK-01..12 | Common candidate; source-first review required before claiming established baseline |\n2719\t   53| | E03 Tool contract compatibility | SK-04; exact a_c and manager implementations | Assessment in progress; native 3.0.1 lifecycle support unresolved |\n2720\t   54| | E04 Codex realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n2721\t   55| | E05 Claude realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n2722\t   56| | E06 Actual host discovery and task behavior | E04/E05; Q01..12 and independent oracle | Required; finite evidence pending |\n2723\t   57| | E07 Independent candidate assessment | Frozen source and E06 evidence | Required for the initial delivery claim; reviewer has no repair authorship |\n2724\t   58| | E08 Delivery disposition and residuals | Current results for E01..07 | Root selects bounded work disposition; Jim retains acceptance/release |\n2725\t   59| \n2726\t   60| Material interface, configuration, lifecycle, authority, recovery, proof and\n2727\t   61| usability concerns are covered through these evaluations and their causal seams.\n2728\t   62| The exact deployed skill package, actual host invocation and tool response form\n2729\t   63| the ordinary proof path. Hosted-service availability, general optimal context\n2730\t   64| selection, statistical model reliability and quantified benefit remain explicit\n2731\t   65| residuals until separately tested. No generic frame family is declared satisfied\n2732\t   66| merely because this table names a nearby concern.\n2733\t   67| \n2734\t   68| ## Conjunction, invalidation and decisions\n2735\t   69| \n2736\t   70| For a claimed capability, all applicable required predicates must have current\n2737\t   71| support on compatible subjects/bases. Unknown applicability remains unresolved;\n2738\t   72| contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting. No implicit\n2739\t   73| translation joins different method or host coordinates. Root may retain valid\n2740\t   74| unaffected evidence and activates only the affected new evaluation after change.\n2741\t   75| \n2742\t   76| Invalidate affected reliance after source/tool/profile/host change, changed\n2743\t   77| authority or scope, a counterexample, failed custody, or a context projection\n2744\t   78| that loses a required future distinction. An uncertain effect is reconciled\n2745\t   79| before retry. Failed construction re-enters the governing owner actually shown\n2746\t   80| to be insufficient; it does not automatically reopen all upstream design.\n2747\t   81| \n2748\t   82| Review severity is S0 catastrophic irreversible harm or systemic unauthorized\n2749\t   83| effects; S1 major authority/basis violation or broadly unusable core outcome;\n2750\t   84| S2 reproducible material functional/semantic failure in a supported ordinary\n2751\t   85| path; S3 bounded defect with a practical workaround or limited consequence;\n2752\t   86| S4 minor clarity/usability issue without demonstrated material outcome failure.\n2753\t   87| The reviewer supplies the effect and evidence supporting that grade. Root assigns\n2754\t   88| work priority and decides the effect on the selected delivery claim separately.\n2755\t   89| A failed mandatory predicate or unresolved authority/effect condition withholds\n2756\t   90| its dependent claim regardless of severity; unrelated observations do not block\n2757\t   91| it. An initial common candidate or a successful test is not owner acceptance.\n2758\t   92| \n2759\t   93| A nonauthor native subagent in the same model family supplies nonauthor evidence\n2760\t   94| with a semantic-independence limitation. It does not establish cross-family\n2761\t   95| independence. The initial final frozen common/tool/skill candidate is selected for\n2762\t   96| an actual fresh Claude review; its exposure and actual resolved model remain\n2763\t   97| part of the retained evidence.\n2764\t   98| \n2765\t   99| Durable activation, result, decision and residual records live under T-001's work\n2766\t  100| surface. A fresh actor can reconstruct the frontier from those records and exact\n2767\t  101| source; chat memory and hidden reasoning are not required evidence.\n2768\t  102| \n2769\t\n2770\t######## [23] product:specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md sel=None ########\n2771\t    1| # Source owners\n2772\t    2| \n2773\t    3| All method references below resolve within the immutable STDO v3.0.1-rc.1\n2774\t    4| installation selected in `stdo_skills.json`, manifest\n2775\t    5| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n2776\t    6| This index routes acquisition; it does not duplicate the clauses or establish\n2777\t    7| that an operation has met them.\n2778\t    8| \n2779\t    9| | Concern | Deciding source within `standards/` |\n2780\t   10| |---|---|\n2781\t   11| | Exact Product and installed basis | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n2782\t   12| | WHAT/HOW separation and tenant binding | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n2783\t   13| | Intake, operation scope, admission and applicability | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n2784\t   14| | Context sufficiency, currentness and acquisition | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n2785\t   15| | Result, exhaustion, effects and disposition | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n2786\t   16| | Role configuration and bounded Executive decisions | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n2787\t   17| | Independent review and acceptance | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n2788\t   18| | Restart, retained results and invalidation | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n2789\t   19| | Cost and proportionality | ACTIVATION.md §6 |\n2790\t   20| | Design and algorithm/computation binding | DESIGN_MODULE.md; SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 10–11 |\n2791\t   21| | Work carriers and condition-based closure | TICKETS.md §§5, 7 |\n2792\t   22| | Actual-path proof and test semantics | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n2793\t   23| | Release identity and consumer adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n2794\t   24| \n2795\t   25| Tenant designs add exact host/tool source references and their verified versions.\n2796\t   26| Host documentation supplies mechanics and cannot alter these methodological\n2797\t   27| contracts. Existing STDO plugin skills and a_c examples are realization donors,\n2798\t   28| with their own declared support limits.\n2799\t   29| \n2800\t\n2801\t######## [24] product:specification/requirements/README.md sel=None ########\n2802\t    1| # Shared requirements\n2803\t    2| \n2804\t    3| Status: common construction candidate. Applies equally to Codex and Claude.\n2805\t    4| Each tenant traces these obligations to its own design, implementation and\n2806\t    5| [scenario evidence](SCENARIOS.md); no identical skill decomposition is required.\n2807\t    6| The exact method owners are indexed in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](../SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\n2808\t    7| \n2809\t    8| ## SK-01: Discoverable task entry\n2810\t    9| \n2811\t   10| In a declared supported host installation, ordinary relevant task requests must\n2812\t   11| make the applicable capability discoverable without requiring the user to remember\n2813\t   12| the skill name. Explicit invocation must work too. Descriptions distinguish\n2814\t   13| governed development from unrelated work. Discovery is tested separately from\n2815\t   14| whether a loaded skill completes the task. Host limits and observed failures are\n2816\t   15| reported instead of claiming guaranteed model compliance.\n2817\t   16| \n2818\t   17| ## SK-02: Static basis and scope\n2819\t   18| \n2820\t   19| The selected Product Definition and exact installed method are resolved and\n2821\t   20| verified before relying on their contracts. Ambiguous, missing or altered bases\n2822\t   21| withhold dependent work. A moving selector, sibling source or retained summary\n2823\t   22| cannot replace the pin. Setup installs or pins only within the supplied grant;\n2824\t   23| ordinary execution never adopts a newer cut implicitly.\n2825\t   24| \n2826\t   25| ## SK-03: Lawful intake and proportional work\n2827\t   26| \n2828\t   27| The skill identifies the required outcome, changed owner and applicable existing\n2829\t   28| work basis, then performs the smallest sufficient authorized work. A small direct\n2830\t   29| task does not automatically acquire a ticket, coordinating actor or reviewer.\n2831\t   30| Material coordination and independent assessment are activated when their actual\n2832\t   31| conditions require them. Existing sufficient authorization is reused without a\n2833\t   32| repeated permission ceremony; missing material authority remains explicit.\n2834\t   33| \n2835\t   34| ## SK-04: Supported tool use\n2836\t   35| \n2837\t   36| Each selected operation has an exact implementation, input/output contract and\n2838\t   37| supported method binding. A declared required tool is actually called; its\n2839\t   38| observed response and effects support the resulting claim. The skill does not\n2840\t   39| replace its outcome with invented checks, a narrative of intended calls, or an\n2841\t   40| unqualified alternate path. Pure construction, assessment, authority and F_P\n2842\t   41| results retain their distinct contracts under 3.0.1.\n2843\t   42| \n2844\t   43| Compatibility is established per operation. A legacy acquisition may supply\n2845\t   44| opaque source bytes under its actual contract; an unsupported lifecycle profile\n2846\t   45| cannot issue 3.0.1 admission or join results by relabeling. A tool failure preserves\n2847\t   46| partial evidence and unknown effects, withholds the dependent claim and identifies\n2848\t   47| the next supported re-entry. Independent useful work may continue within its grant.\n2849\t   48| \n2850\t   49| ## SK-05: Adequate bounded context\n2851\t   50| \n2852\t   51| Context retains the exact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority,\n2853\t   52| required evidence, capability limits, return consumer and invalidators needed for\n2854\t   53| the task. It is acquired through current source routes and may use verified\n2855\t   54| derived views. Equal candidate bytes do not erase differing retained assessments,\n2856\t   55| unresolved obligations or currentness facts that require different continuations.\n2857\t   56| No general optimal-compression claim follows from a sufficient task context.\n2858\t   57| \n2859\t   58| ## SK-06: Construction and delegated return\n2860\t   59| \n2861\t   60| Direct or delegated workers receive the governing requirement/design, exact\n2862\t   61| operation grant and territory, applicable proof predicates and bounded return.\n2863\t   62| Delegation preserves these bindings across the actual host handoff. A child\n2864\t   63| completion does not start an unrequested stage. Actor output, transport success,\n2865\t   64| candidate availability, assessment and acceptance remain distinguishable.\n2866\t   65| \n2867\t   66| ## SK-07: Independent review\n2868\t   67| \n2869\t   68| Where required, the reviewer derives expectations from governing sources before\n2870\t   69| evaluating the exact candidate and proof. The reviewer reports actual exposure,\n2871\t   70| evidence, severity and affected claims; it does not author the adopted repair or\n2872\t   71| assume acceptance authority. A different role label alone proves no independence.\n2873\t   72| Required fresh assessment after material change cannot be replaced by a stale\n2874\t   73| review result.\n2875\t   74| \n2876\t   75| ## SK-08: Continuation and recovery\n2877\t   76| \n2878\t   77| On resume or interrupted execution, acquire material current state and reconcile\n2879\t   78| observed effects before retry. Retain unresolved obligations and valid evidence;\n2880\t   79| invalidate only affected reliance with its reason. Distinguish no assessment,\n2881\t   80| performed indeterminate assessment and incomplete construction. A timeout does\n2882\t   81| not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not duplicate an uncertain effect.\n2883\t   82| \n2884\t   83| ## SK-09: Truthful status and closure\n2885\t   84| \n2886\t   85| Status names what was constructed, assessed and decided, including exact subject,\n2887\t   86| basis, evidence and remaining work. Closure follows applicable predicates and\n2888\t   87| required dispositions, not test count, review occurrence or a fluent summary.\n2889\t   88| An unsupported or unperformed case remains visible, never a passing result.\n2890\t   89| \n2891\t   90| ## SK-10: Release and installation\n2892\t   91| \n2893\t   92| Release skills bind the exact selected candidate, release conditions, publication\n2894\t   93| grant and destination, using the supported release tools. They can prepare a\n2895\t   94| reviewable release without inferring publication authority. They preserve the\n2896\t   95| method's immutable-cut semantics and keep installation/adoption decisions explicit.\n2897\t   96| Installation into one host must not silently enable the other tenant or change\n2898\t   97| unrelated user configuration. An upgrade retains the ability to identify the\n2899\t   98| previous package and deliberately replace or remove the selected installation.\n2900\t   99| \n2901\t  100| ## SK-11: Independent realization and maintenance\n2902\t  101| \n2903\t  102| Each tenant declares its requirements-to-algorithms and algorithms-to-host\n2904\t  103| bindings, supported versions, failure behavior and qualification scope. Shared\n2905\t  104| mechanics are consumed rather than reimplemented without a supported distinction.\n2906\t  105| Tuning is driven by observed task behavior. Host changes, tool-contract changes\n2907\t  106| and method adoption identify affected tests and claims without resetting unrelated\n2908\t  107| valid evidence. Skill/source references remain resolvable in the delivered form.\n2909\t  108| \n2910\t  109| ## SK-12: Evidence and benefit\n2911\t  110| \n2912\t  111| Qualification uses common task semantics, independent expected outcomes and the\n2913\t  112| actual public host/tool paths. Retain actual invocation, acquired inputs, outputs,\n2914\t  113| tool traces, observed effects, elapsed time and reported token/cost data; unavailable\n2915\t  114| measures remain unknown. Compare equivalent substantive information and count\n2916\t  115| retries, repair and review in total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence,\n2917\t  116| not statistical reliability or general benefit. Keyword and formatting checks\n2918\t  117| may establish structure but not successful method application.\n2919\t  118| \n2920\t\n2921\t######## [25] product:specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md sel=None ########\n2922\t    1| # Common qualification scenarios\n2923\t    2| \n2924\t    3| This is the shared oracle specification. Tenant implementations may use different\n2925\t    4| skill names and host mechanisms. Execute the same substantive tasks, authorities\n2926\t    5| and expected outcomes on both hosts; retain the exact tenant and tool cuts.\n2927\t    6| \n2928\t    7| ## Protocol\n2929\t    8| \n2930\t    9| For each case, freeze a small isolated workspace with a Product Definition, the\n2931\t   10| selected method, relevant source and an explicit effect grant where needed.\n2932\t   11| Derive expected outcomes from the common requirement before acquiring the tenant's\n2933\t   12| answer. Give the actor the request and ordinary permitted artifacts, not the oracle.\n2934\t   13| Run automatic-discovery and explicit-invocation lanes separately. Freeze model,\n2935\t   14| host version, settings, source exposure, resource bound and any environmental\n2936\t   15| differences. A fallback invocation after automatic failure is another attempt.\n2937\t   16| \n2938\t   17| Record actual host/tool events, material postimages and the actor's final result.\n2939\t   18| Assess the outcome and required path together. Missing traces or unavailable host\n2940\t   19| capability leave that claim unestablished. Every failed attempt remains in the\n2941\t   20| record. One completed run per mandatory case/host is the minimum finite witness;\n2942\t   21| it is not an estimated success rate. Repetitions for reliability or cost comparison\n2943\t   22| need a separately selected sample plan. A larger suite is unnecessary absent a\n2944\t   23| new failure or material change.\n2945\t   24| \n2946\t   25| ## Cases and falsifiers\n2947\t   26| \n2948\t   27| | Case | Ordinary task and controlled distinction | Required observation and falsifier | Requirements |\n2949\t   28| |---|---|---|---|\n2950\t   29| | Q01 | Ask to perform a bounded STDO workspace change without naming a skill; then run equivalent fresh explicit invocation | Actual skill acquisition and required tool calls lead to the requested change; failure to discover is reported separately from execution failure | SK-01, 03, 04, 12 |\n2951\t   30| | Q02 | Ask an unrelated factual or non-governed task | No forced STDO setup, new work carrier or irrelevant tool sequence | SK-01, 03 |\n2952\t   31| | Q03 | Resolve a valid pinned workspace; in isolated variants remove the install, alter one installed member, and introduce ambiguous Product selection | Valid case uses exact verified cut; each invalid case withholds only dependent effects and identifies the cause, never substitutes latest or sibling source | SK-02 |\n2953\t   32| | Q04 | Authorized one-file correction with sufficient existing requirement/design and direct Writer scope | Correct change and focused evidence without invented mandatory ticket, coordination or review; no write outside scope | SK-03, 06 |\n2954\t   33| | Q05 | A change requiring one bounded worker and independent review | Actual handoff preserves basis/grant/return; reviewer acquires deciding sources and exact candidate; Executive consumes results before next activation | SK-05, 06, 07 |\n2955\t   34| | Q06 | Present a tool that returns unsupported method and one that returns an execution error | Actual refusal/error retained; no manufactured success, silent bypass or semantic conclusion from transport; next supported re-entry identified | SK-04, 09 |\n2956\t   35| | Q07 | Resume two histories with identical candidate bytes: one has a current accepted assessment, one has an unresolved counterexample invalidating that assessment | Continuations differ as required; the retained obligation cannot disappear into an identical candidate-only summary | SK-05, 08, 09 |\n2957\t   36| | Q08 | Interrupt a bounded effect after its target changes but before acknowledgment; resume with the same work instruction | Reacquires the target and reconciles evidence before retry; no duplicated effect or claim that timeout proves rollback | SK-04, 08 |\n2958\t   37| | Q09 | Give an old passing review, then materially change the governed source or candidate | Affected reliance is withdrawn and missing reassessment stays open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable | SK-07, 08, 09 |\n2959\t   38| | Q10 | Exhaust construction before a candidate; perform an inconclusive assessment in another case; leave assessment unperformed in a third | Candidate availability, indeterminate assessment and no assessment are reported with the correct predicate and residual; no universal exhausted verdict | SK-08, 09 |\n2960\t   39| | Q11 | Request release preparation with a local artifact grant and no remote publication grant; then separately exercise an authorized isolated local deployment | Exact reviewable candidate and destination; no unauthorized publication, no invented second final cut, verified local installed result on authorized path | SK-10 |\n2961\t   40| | Q12 | Install, invoke and remove one tenant in a disposable host workspace; repeat after a compatible package update | Host discovers exact selected package, referenced files resolve, update identity is visible, removal is scoped and the other tenant/unrelated config remains intact | SK-01, 10, 11 |\n2962\t   41| \n2963\t   42| ## Assessment record\n2964\t   43| \n2965\t   44| Each record binds case, lane, tenant/package and host/model identities, inputs and\n2966\t   45| authority, expected predicates, actual result and tool path, effect evidence,\n2967\t   46| verdict per predicate, unresolved claims, measured/unknown costs and invalidators.\n2968\t   47| Semantically assess unexpected behavior; a checker must not grade success solely\n2969\t   48| from the presence of a named command or required phrase.\n2970\t   49| \n2971\t   50| Initial delivery claims each mandatory case separately. A failed or absent case\n2972\t   51| withholds that tenant's affected supported capability. The Executive may select a\n2973\t   52| smaller explicitly stated delivery claim only within the owner's outcome; it may\n2974\t   53| not erase a required capability by renaming a failed case optional.\n2975\t   54| \n2976\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"98a7fcfa-4f3c-4aa2-b558-f535c8a3b7ba","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:12:40.430Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","content":"######## [14] product:.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md sel=None ########\n    1| # T-001 — Build STDO Skills with STDO 3.0.1 and current tools\n    2| \n    3| Status: active construction; common source is a candidate. Product acceptance,\n    4| publication and general benefit remain open.\n    5| \n    6| ## Owner instruction\n    7| \n    8| The owner first selected a separate root-level `stdo_skills/` Product, shared\n    9| requirements, and independent Codex and Claude skill build tenants tuned to their\n   10| hosts. The immediate concrete proposal named `stdo_skills.json`, common\n   11| `specification/` and `build_tenants/{codex,claude}/` with designs, skills and tests.\n   12| Jim then instructed:\n   13| \n   14| > yes the are decoupled, this is a test, eating our own dog food,\n   15| > 1. pin stdo 3.0.1 as the static released methodology against specification_method\n   16| > 2. as executive build out of stdo skills, use the current tooling to build the skills\n   17| \n   18| This binds the construction outcome and method selection. It does not accept\n   19| documents yet to be written or authorize remote publication or global deployment.\n   20| \n   21| ## Work basis and current admission interpretation\n   22| \n   23| The static methodology is `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n   24| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`;\n   25| native commit `fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9`.\n   26| The isolated source worktree is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills`,\n   27| branch `codex/stdo-skills`, initial repository base\n   28| `a2e56d8bd2882068c84e45b2423cecc246c62525`.\n   29| \n   30| Root's Writer activation selects the exact proposed construction and bounded\n   31| territory under the recorded owner instruction. Root explicitly directs the\n   32| initial Writer to consume that existing human authorization and create a\n   33| reviewable common candidate, without claiming a deterministic admission result.\n   34| This is the bounded construction interpretation used here. It is not a fabricated\n   35| human override of a later unseen contract, a tool-issued admission, an accepted\n   36| Project frame basis or proof of completed STDO application.\n   37| \n   38| ACTIVATION §1 Admission requires exact-contract admission evidence for governed\n   39| execution. Integration of that requirement with subsequent real delegated\n   40| operation contracts is an open tool/application obligation, E03, and must be\n   41| resolved before claiming the native supported lifecycle path. Recording a drafted\n   42| contract or this ticket cannot supply that evidence. Any review disagreement\n   43| about the initial construction interpretation remains attached to these effects;\n   44| it cannot be erased by a later successful test.\n   45| \n   46| ## Outcome and decision scope\n   47| \n   48| Deliver independently designed and usable Codex/Claude skill packages against\n   49| common requirements, static methodology and actual supported tools. Root is the\n   50| Executive: it keeps the outcome/frontier, selects bounded requirements/design\n   51| candidates for construction, allocates Writer operations, assesses closed returns\n   52| and orders supported repairs. Product acceptance/release and changed Product\n   53| meaning remain with Jim. Root does not mutate while occupying Executive.\n   54| \n   55| Common documents and the frame configuration remain candidates until an exact\n   56| Root construction disposition is recorded. That disposition supplies only the\n   57| decisions covered by Root's grant; it is not owner acceptance or a substitute\n   58| for required execution admission.\n   59| \n   60| ## Territory and effects\n   61| \n   62| - Bootstrap Writer: isolated worktree creation, exact static installation,\n   63|   `stdo_skills.json` and bootstrap evidence; no adoption into existing Products.\n   64| - Common Writer: this ticket, Product README/AGENTS/CLAUDE, `specification/`,\n   65|   `build_tenants/README.md` and `.ai-workspace/work/T001/common/` only.\n   66| - Tenant Writers: their separately bound `build_tenants/codex/` or `claude/`\n   67|   territory and named evidence surfaces, after Root activation.\n   68| - Qualification: disposable declared workspaces and exact retained evidence,\n   69|   with actual host/model/resource settings recorded before execution.\n   70| - a_c repairs: separately bounded owner territory and supported contract change;\n   71|   no tenant silently forks tool semantics. No modification of released STDO.\n   72| \n   73| Preserve unrelated worktrees and files. No commit, push, remote publication or\n   74| global skill configuration change follows from a common Writer or tenant grant.\n   75| Any later checkpoint/distribution operation needs its exact existing scope bound.\n   76| \n   77| ## Execution plan and ledger\n   78| \n   79| | Stage | Required result | Current standing |\n   80| |---|---|---|\n   81| | 1. Pin | Installed 3.0.1 integrity and definition binding | Bootstrap evidence retained; common Writer independently observed valid verification |\n   82| | 2. Common WHAT | Intent, Product, requirements, scenarios and frame proposal | Candidate delivered for Root disposition and review |\n   83| | 3. Tool binding | Per-operation 3.0.1 support or exact justified translation, including admission | Current-tool assessment in progress; RC9 lifecycle support does not establish this |\n   84| | 4. Tenant design/build | Independent Codex and Claude HOW with requirement trace and runnable packages | Pending respective bounded activations |\n   85| | 5. Actual use | Common Q01..12 outcomes and actual tool-path evidence on both hosts | Not performed by this common Writer |\n   86| | 6. Independent assessment | Exact candidates, source-derived oracle, findings and supported repairs | Pending |\n   87| | 7. Delivery disposition | Truthful supported claims, effects and residuals | Pending; no release selected |\n   88| \n   89| Use the smallest dependency-ready frontier. Common-source review and host-design\n   90| preparation may proceed while tool compatibility is resolved; operations that\n   91| depend on unsupported contracts remain withheld. No task is restarted merely\n   92| because another role is activated. A demonstrated counterexample determines the\n   93| affected re-entry and scope of repair.\n   94| \n   95| ## Proof and closure\n   96| \n   97| The durable result/evidence surface is `.ai-workspace/work/T001/`.\n   98| The common Writer's exact inventory, source/tool observations, structural checks\n   99| and return are under `common/`. Bootstrap retains actual installer evidence under\n  100| `bootstrap/`. Later activations append their own exact-source results and costs.\n  101| \n  102| The [common scenarios](../../../specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md) define\n  103| observable predicates, not expected wording. The initial delivery claim requires\n  104| both usable tenant implementations, supported declared tool paths, mandatory\n  105| finite scenario evidence and independent assessment with supported repairs.\n  106| Missing results, changed bases, unknown effects or unresolved required conditions\n  107| withhold affected closure. Metadata validation and test totals alone cannot close\n  108| the Product outcome. Root reports partial results honestly if a resource or\n  109| authority boundary stops work.\n  110| \n  111| ## Re-entry and stop conditions\n  112| \n  113| Re-enter the relevant owner for missing or changed Product meaning, unsupported\n  114| tool semantics, insufficient context, actual host capability mismatch, invalid\n  115| source custody, or a counterexample to required behavior. Reconcile uncertain\n  116| effects before retry. Retain open obligations and prior attempts. Stop the\n  117| dependent operation for missing authority, an unresolved hard boundary, exhausted\n  118| declared envelope or an unsupported contract. Continue unrelated authorized work\n  119| where its basis remains sufficient.\n  120| \n  121| No failure or review result changes the static method pin. A proposed new method\n  122| adoption, Product scope change or publication returns to Jim with its concrete\n  123| consequences. Routine implementation choices and supported repairs stay within\n  124| the selected construction mandate.\n  125| \n\n######## [15] product:AGENTS.md sel=None ########\n    1| # STDO Skills bootstrap\n    2| \n    3| Select `stdo_skills.json`, verify its exact installed basis with `stdo status\n    4| --definition stdo_skills.json --verify`, and read the declared bootstrap and\n    5| deciding owner sections from that installation. The operative cut is STDO\n    6| v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n    7| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n    8| Do not adopt a newer cut from the discovery selector implicitly.\n    9| \n   10| Read README, Intent, Product, Goals, requirements and the current frame-basis\n   11| disposition. Common WHAT belongs in `specification/`. Codex and Claude are\n   12| independent HOW tenants, each with its own design and skills. Shared requirements\n   13| do not require identical prompts, decomposition or host machinery.\n   14| \n   15| The initial common documents are candidates for Executive construction\n   16| disposition. Their presence and the Product Definition locator are not evidence\n   17| of acceptance. T-001 records the owner's concrete construction instruction and\n   18| the current admission/tooling limitation.\n   19| \n   20| Executive coordinates; it does not mutate. A separately bound Worker/Writer\n   21| performs exact named effects. Use bounded delegation for material context,\n   22| capability or independence boundaries. A sufficient small task may use direct\n   23| Writer entry without automatic tickets or independent review. Reviewers acquire\n   24| source-derived expectations and the exact candidate independently and return\n   25| findings; they do not implement repairs or decide promotion.\n   26| \n   27| Use the declared supported tool contracts and retain actual responses. Required\n   28| tool failure or an unsupported method binding withholds its dependent claim;\n   29| do not simulate a passing result or silently bypass the required path. Preserve\n   30| unrelated work and the frozen released methodology. Native tools and actor calls\n   31| are mechanisms, not new admission, acceptance or release authority.\n   32| \n\n######## [16] product:CLAUDE.md sel=None ########\n    1| # STDO Skills bootstrap\n    2| \n    3| Select `stdo_skills.json`, verify its exact installed basis with `stdo status\n    4| --definition stdo_skills.json --verify`, and read the declared bootstrap and\n    5| deciding owner sections from that installation. The operative cut is STDO\n    6| v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n    7| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n    8| Do not adopt a newer cut from the discovery selector implicitly.\n    9| \n   10| Read README, Intent, Product, Goals, requirements and the current frame-basis\n   11| disposition. Common WHAT belongs in `specification/`. Codex and Claude are\n   12| independent HOW tenants, each with its own design and skills. Shared requirements\n   13| do not require identical prompts, decomposition or host machinery.\n   14| \n   15| The initial common documents are candidates for Executive construction\n   16| disposition. Their presence and the Product Definition locator are not evidence\n   17| of acceptance. T-001 records the owner's concrete construction instruction and\n   18| the current admission/tooling limitation.\n   19| \n   20| Executive coordinates; it does not mutate. A separately bound Worker/Writer\n   21| performs exact named effects. Use bounded delegation for material context,\n   22| capability or independence boundaries. A sufficient small task may use direct\n   23| Writer entry without automatic tickets or independent review. Reviewers acquire\n   24| source-derived expectations and the exact candidate independently and return\n   25| findings; they do not implement repairs or decide promotion.\n   26| \n   27| Use the declared supported tool contracts and retain actual responses. Required\n   28| tool failure or an unsupported method binding withholds its dependent claim;\n   29| do not simulate a passing result or silently bypass the required path. Preserve\n   30| unrelated work and the frozen released methodology. Native tools and actor calls\n   31| are mechanisms, not new admission, acceptance or release authority.\n   32| \n\n######## [17] product:README.md sel=None ########\n    1| # STDO Skills\n    2| \n    3| STDO Skills makes the selected STDO method usable in ordinary agent work through\n    4| tool-backed skills. One shared specification has two independent build tenants:\n    5| Codex and Claude. Each tenant may choose different skill boundaries, instructions,\n    6| context mechanisms and host integration while preserving the same requirements.\n    7| \n    8| This is a construction candidate. The current work is [T-001](.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\n    9| Read [Intent](specification/INTENT.md), [Product](specification/PRODUCT.md),\n   10| [Goals](specification/GOALS.md), [requirements](specification/requirements/README.md)\n   11| and the [frame basis](specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md).\n   12| \n   13| The static methodology is **STDO 3.0.1 RC1**, selected by\n   14| [stdo_skills.json](stdo_skills.json). Its manifest is\n   15| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n   16| The discovery selector never substitutes for that operative basis.\n   17| \n   18| ```sh\n   19| stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify\n   20| ```\n   21| \n   22| STDO owns methodology; a_c owns computational support tools; this Product owns\n   23| the agent-facing application of those contracts. Their release and adoption\n   24| decisions remain separate. Existing installed STDO skills are donor material,\n   25| not the new tenants' accepted implementation.\n   26| \n   27| Current a_c lifecycle tooling has a Claude RC9 method binding. Its support for\n   28| 3.0.1 must be established per operation. An honest legacy mechanical acquisition\n   29| can supply source bytes; it does not establish 3.0.1 lifecycle admission,\n   30| conjunction or semantic qualification. See the\n   31| [tool-binding requirement](specification/requirements/README.md#sk-04-supported-tool-use).\n   32| \n   33| The initial proof is a matched finite set of realistic tasks on both hosts,\n   34| including automatic discovery, explicit invocation, tool failures and recovery.\n   35| Passing metadata checks alone does not show that agents use the tooling.\n   36| \n\n######## [18] product:build_tenants/README.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Skill build tenants\n    2| \n    3| | Tenant | Target execution environment | Owned realization |\n    4| |---|---|---|\n    5| | `codex` | Declared Codex host/version and model/settings | Codex design, skill decomposition, prompts, supporting resources, installation and qualification |\n    6| | `claude` | Declared Claude host/version and model/settings | Claude design, skill decomposition, prompts, supporting resources, installation and qualification |\n    7| \n    8| Both implement [the same requirements](../specification/requirements/README.md)\n    9| under the Product's pinned STDO 3.0.1 basis. Each design must show its calculus\n   10| binding from requirements to operations and its execution binding to the actual\n   11| host, including material effects, failure behavior and resource assumptions.\n   12| \n   13| Tenant differences require a supported host or behavioral reason. Shared contract\n   14| meaning is not copied and independently changed in prompt text. Skill names,\n   15| counts and wording may differ; qualification compares outcomes and required paths.\n   16| Existing STDO plugin skills may be selected as exact donors, then revised as the\n   17| requirements demand. No donor inherits acceptance into this Product.\n   18| \n   19| The public surface for each tenant includes its install/discovery route, explicit\n   20| invocation, ordinary task behavior, supported tools and removal/update behavior.\n   21| Keep host mechanics in tenant HOW and tool algorithms with their existing owner.\n   22| Do not invent a shared skill runtime to make the directories symmetrical.\n   23| \n   24| Construction remains isolated to the tenant's granted territory. Shared WHAT\n   25| changes return to Root. A review identifies its exact candidate and exposure;\n   26| one tenant's success supplies no qualification for the other host.\n   27| \n\n######## [19] product:specification/GOALS.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Goals\n    2| \n    3| ## Current selection\n    4| \n    5| [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md) constructs the new\n    6| STDO Skills Product using static released STDO 3.0.1 RC1 and current tooling.\n    7| The common WHAT is shared; Codex and Claude receive independently designed and\n    8| tuned build tenants. This is the initial practical test of the method on its own\n    9| agent tooling.\n   10| \n   11| Current common documents are candidates awaiting Root's exact construction\n   12| disposition. Bootstrap installed-basis verification is evidence about the basis,\n   13| not proof of the skills. Tool compatibility assessment is in progress.\n   14| \n   15| ## Delivery outcomes\n   16| \n   17| 1. Verify the immutable method pin and preserve it throughout construction.\n   18| 2. Establish common capabilities, discriminators, frame basis and work authority.\n   19| 3. Resolve the tool contracts required by the selected lifecycle paths.\n   20| 4. Construct independent Codex and Claude designs and working skill packages.\n   21| 5. Exercise matched finite scenarios on actual hosts and inspect actual tool calls.\n   22| 6. Obtain independent assessment, repair supported defects and present a bounded\n   23|    delivery result with all remaining limitations.\n   24| \n   25| The [T-001 ledger](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md#execution-plan-and-ledger)\n   26| owns detailed progress. Publication, fleet deployment, global default changes and\n   27| general efficiency claims are outside the initial delivery result.\n   28| \n\n######## [20] product:specification/INTENT.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Intent\n    2| \n    3| Make STDO usable through skills that help agents choose and perform the right\n    4| work with the available computational tools. Reduce repeated ad hoc context\n    5| construction, omitted checks and recovery mistakes while preserving the owner's\n    6| outcome and the methodology's distinctions.\n    7| \n    8| Build one common Product with independently tuned Codex and Claude realizations.\n    9| Keep the released STDO 3.0.1 methodology static during this experiment. Use the\n   10| method and current tools to build the skills, exposing real integration gaps as\n   11| evidence rather than explaining them away.\n   12| \n   13| Demonstrate actual tool use and useful outcomes on declared tasks before claiming\n   14| effective operation. Efficiency improvement and reliable automatic selection are\n   15| empirical claims to measure, not consequences of packaging instructions as skills.\n   16| \n\n######## [21] product:specification/PRODUCT.md sel=None ########\n    1| # STDO Skills\n    2| \n    3| Status: common construction candidate under T-001; not Product acceptance or release.\n    4| \n    5| ## Product boundary\n    6| \n    7| Product identity: `urn:stdo:product-definition:stdo-skills`.\n    8| Bounded context: `urn:stdo-skills:bounded-context:agent-method-application`.\n    9| \n   10| The Product supplies skills for F_P agents applying an exactly selected STDO\n   11| methodology to software-development work. It connects recognizable user tasks\n   12| to the deciding source, appropriate context, supported tool operations and\n   13| observable returns. It owns requirements for this user-facing capability and\n   14| evidence that each tenant realizes it.\n   15| \n   16| STDO owns the method. a_c and other declared Development Products own their tool\n   17| contracts and computational implementations. A skill preserves and applies those\n   18| contracts; it does not create another lifecycle, state store or source of\n   19| assessment, admission, acceptance or publication authority.\n   20| \n   21| ## Selected methodology\n   22| \n   23| The complete static builder and initial supported methodology is\n   24| `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\n   25| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n   26| Native commit: `fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9`;\n   27| package: `specification_methodology/v3`.\n   28| The [Product Definition](../stdo_skills.json) owns the operative locator.\n   29| The mutable `3.0.1` discovery channel is not an adoption instruction.\n   30| \n   31| The release remains static while this Product's requirements, designs and skills\n   32| are developed. A later method adoption requires an explicit compatibility\n   33| decision and affected qualification; an implementation defect does not authorize\n   34| editing the selected methodology.\n   35| \n   36| ## Users and capability\n   37| \n   38| The user works in a governed workspace using Codex or Claude. Skills support:\n   39| \n   40| - setup and exact Product/method selection;\n   41| - intake and re-entry at the changed requirement, design or realization owner;\n   42| - context acquisition and bounded frame construction;\n   43| - authorized direct work or Executive-directed delegation;\n   44| - source-first independent review where required;\n   45| - continuation, recovery, currentness and truthful status;\n   46| - release preparation and separately authorized release operations.\n   47| \n   48| The shared requirements state outcomes and discriminators. They do not prescribe\n   49| skill count, names, prompt identity, invocation syntax or host-specific mechanism.\n   50| Each tenant owns its computational and execution binding, including instructions,\n   51| supporting references, tool integration, installation and tuning.\n   52| \n   53| ## Tool relationship\n   54| \n   55| The current `stdo` manager can verify and resolve the exact installation. Existing\n   56| a_c mechanics are available through an explicitly selected implementation and\n   57| method binding. The current legacy lifecycle profile is not renamed to 3.0.1.\n   58| Each operation used for a 3.0.1 claim needs established compatibility or a declared\n   59| supported translation. Reading opaque source bytes under an honestly identified\n   60| legacy acquisition contract makes only that acquisition claim.\n   61| \n   62| Tool harmonisation remains owned by a_c. This Product may identify required\n   63| contracts, report defects and consume a supported increment; it does not fork\n   64| tool semantics into each tenant. A skill's direct use of host facilities must\n   65| be declared in its design, preserve the selected operation contract and be\n   66| qualified on that actual path. It cannot substitute for a required tool result.\n   67| \n   68| F_D classification follows the selected calculus's totality and dependency\n   69| requirements. An F_D constructor gains no assessment or admission authority from\n   70| that classification; invoking an F_P actor does not make its semantic answer\n   71| deterministic. The deciding owners are in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\n   72| \n   73| ## Independent tenants and releases\n   74| \n   75| `build_tenants/codex/` and `build_tenants/claude/` independently realize the common\n   76| WHAT. Evidence and supported-host claims are tenant-specific. Both use the same\n   77| task semantics and acceptance predicates, while host realization and tuning may\n   78| differ materially. Common machinery is reused where its contract fits; retained\n   79| variants need a concrete supported difference.\n   80| \n   81| This Product is a peer at the monorepo root. It has its own lifecycle and release\n   82| identity and is not automatically a member of an existing STDO release cohort.\n   83| The present work constructs candidates and performs bounded qualification; it\n   84| does not publish a release or install skills into unrelated user environments.\n   85| \n   86| ## Construction authority\n   87| \n   88| Jim owns Product scope, common meaning, acceptance and release. His recorded\n   89| [T-001 instruction](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md#owner-instruction)\n   90| selects this Product, its two tenants, static method and Executive-directed\n   91| construction. Root is the bounded Executive for that work and can select\n   92| requirements/design candidates for construction, allocate exact Writer effects,\n   93| evaluate returns, request supported repairs and retain residuals within that\n   94| outcome. It cannot silently broaden Product meaning or claim owner acceptance.\n   95| \n   96| The current [frame basis](REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md) is proposed for this\n   97| construction. Its disposition must be recorded against exact candidate bytes.\n   98| The owner's work authorization, a drafted execution contract, deterministic\n   99| admission and acceptance remain distinct. T-001 records the initial construction\n  100| interpretation and the unresolved integration of later admission contracts.\n  101| \n  102| ## Acceptance boundary\n  103| \n  104| Initial delivery requires a coherent common specification, both realized tenant\n  105| designs, usable host installation paths, supported tool bindings, and independent\n  106| assessment of the [finite scenario evidence](requirements/SCENARIOS.md).\n  107| Missing or failed mandatory evidence withholds the corresponding supported claim.\n  108| It cannot be hidden by a suite total or by the other tenant succeeding.\n  109| \n  110| Repeated use may establish broader reliability and benefit. This first experiment\n  111| supports only the cases, hosts, settings, tool versions and outcomes actually\n  112| observed. Product acceptance and release remain owner decisions on that evidence.\n  113| \n\n######## [22] product:specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Project reference-frame basis\n    2| \n    3| Identity: `urn:stdo-skills:frame-basis:initial:1`.\n    4| Status: proposed construction configuration; Root disposition over its exact\n    5| bytes is pending. The Product Definition points here as its intended basis;\n    6| that pointer does not establish acceptance.\n    7| \n    8| ## Method, outcome and authority\n    9| \n   10| The complete method is STDO v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n   11| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n   12| Read the exact installed REFERENCE_FRAME and ACTIVATION owners. This configuration\n   13| applies the Executive/Worker/Reviewer relations of EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10,\n   14| 12 and 16 to the owner's selected dogfood construction, while retaining the\n   15| sufficient direct Writer branch. It makes no claim of completed profile\n   16| qualification or automatic applicability of every available specialist frame.\n   17| \n   18| The governed mutable source is this `stdo_skills/` Product. The outcome is two\n   19| usable skill tenants satisfying the common requirements and assessed on the\n   20| finite declared tasks. Jim owns Product acceptance and release. Root's bounded\n   21| construction decisions and exact user instruction are in [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\n   22| An actor label supplies no effect grant or admission. The initial construction\n   23| interpretation and subsequent admission obligation remain explicit there.\n   24| \n   25| ## Frames and coordinates\n   26| \n   27| | Frame | Evaluation and material attention | Authority, evidence and return |\n   28| |---|---|---|\n   29| | Executive `skills.executive/1` | Exact Product outcome, dependency-ready frontier, current candidate identities, closed returns, tool compatibility and remaining claims | Select only authorized bounded actions; no mutation in this frame; consumes source-bound returns and records decisions through a granted Writer |\n   30| | Worker `skills.worker/1` | Exact requirement/design, affected producers/consumers, selected host/tool contracts, operation territory and proof predicates | Construct only within grant; self-review and return exact candidate, performed/unperformed evaluations, effects, residuals and invalidators to Executive |\n   31| | Reviewer `skills.reviewer/1` | Source-derived expected behavior, exact frozen candidate and actual-path evidence, exposure history and test semantics | Independent assessment, not repair or promotion; return findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty to Executive |\n   32| | Direct Writer `skills.direct-writer/1` | One sufficient local outcome, existing basis and effect grant, current preimage and focused proof | No coordination or independent review added solely from task existence; admission and exact territory still required; return to declared consumer |\n   33| \n   34| Each activation names frame/revision, exact evaluation/result algebra, subject and\n   35| basis, material invariants, authorities, evidence/tools, capability/context\n   36| envelope, exclusions, dependencies, consumer and stop/re-entry conditions, as\n   37| REFERENCE_FRAME §11 requires. File identities use content hashes or exact commits;\n   38| host/model settings and tool/profile versions are material coordinates. Results\n   39| use ACTIVATION's work/result refinements with named predicates, not an invented\n   40| local pass algebra.\n   41| \n   42| No actor receives the entire repository merely because it is available. The\n   43| Executive selects the deciding frontier. Workers acquire the causal cone needed\n   44| for their own change; Reviewers acquire sources independently. Measured task\n   45| context, actor capability and remaining unknowns accompany each activation.\n   46| \n   47| ## Known evaluation inventory and coverage\n   48| \n   49| | Evaluation | Source and dependency | Current disposition |\n   50| |---|---|---|\n   51| | E01 Exact static method and definition | Product selection; manager verification | Bootstrap evidence available; definition completion remains tied to common disposition |\n   52| | E02 Common outcome and requirement adequacy | Intent, Product, SK-01..12 | Common candidate; source-first review required before claiming established baseline |\n   53| | E03 Tool contract compatibility | SK-04; exact a_c and manager implementations | Assessment in progress; native 3.0.1 lifecycle support unresolved |\n   54| | E04 Codex realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n   55| | E05 Claude realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n   56| | E06 Actual host discovery and task behavior | E04/E05; Q01..12 and independent oracle | Required; finite evidence pending |\n   57| | E07 Independent candidate assessment | Frozen source and E06 evidence | Required for the initial delivery claim; reviewer has no repair authorship |\n   58| | E08 Delivery disposition and residuals | Current results for E01..07 | Root selects bounded work disposition; Jim retains acceptance/release |\n   59| \n   60| Material interface, configuration, lifecycle, authority, recovery, proof and\n   61| usability concerns are covered through these evaluations and their causal seams.\n   62| The exact deployed skill package, actual host invocation and tool response form\n   63| the ordinary proof path. Hosted-service availability, general optimal context\n   64| selection, statistical model reliability and quantified benefit remain explicit\n   65| residuals until separately tested. No generic frame family is declared satisfied\n   66| merely because this table names a nearby concern.\n   67| \n   68| ## Conjunction, invalidation and decisions\n   69| \n   70| For a claimed capability, all applicable required predicates must have current\n   71| support on compatible subjects/bases. Unknown applicability remains unresolved;\n   72| contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting. No implicit\n   73| translation joins different method or host coordinates. Root may retain valid\n   74| unaffected evidence and activates only the affected new evaluation after change.\n   75| \n   76| Invalidate affected reliance after source/tool/profile/host change, changed\n   77| authority or scope, a counterexample, failed custody, or a context projection\n   78| that loses a required future distinction. An uncertain effect is reconciled\n   79| before retry. Failed construction re-enters the governing owner actually shown\n   80| to be insufficient; it does not automatically reopen all upstream design.\n   81| \n   82| Review severity is S0 catastrophic irreversible harm or systemic unauthorized\n   83| effects; S1 major authority/basis violation or broadly unusable core outcome;\n   84| S2 reproducible material functional/semantic failure in a supported ordinary\n   85| path; S3 bounded defect with a practical workaround or limited consequence;\n   86| S4 minor clarity/usability issue without demonstrated material outcome failure.\n   87| The reviewer supplies the effect and evidence supporting that grade. Root assigns\n   88| work priority and decides the effect on the selected delivery claim separately.\n   89| A failed mandatory predicate or unresolved authority/effect condition withholds\n   90| its dependent claim regardless of severity; unrelated observations do not block\n   91| it. An initial common candidate or a successful test is not owner acceptance.\n   92| \n   93| A nonauthor native subagent in the same model family supplies nonauthor evidence\n   94| with a semantic-independence limitation. It does not establish cross-family\n   95| independence. The initial final frozen common/tool/skill candidate is selected for\n   96| an actual fresh Claude review; its exposure and actual resolved model remain\n   97| part of the retained evidence.\n   98| \n   99| Durable activation, result, decision and residual records live under T-001's work\n  100| surface. A fresh actor can reconstruct the frontier from those records and exact\n  101| source; chat memory and hidden reasoning are not required evidence.\n  102| \n\n######## [23] product:specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Source owners\n    2| \n    3| All method references below resolve within the immutable STDO v3.0.1-rc.1\n    4| installation selected in `stdo_skills.json`, manifest\n    5| `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\n    6| This index routes acquisition; it does not duplicate the clauses or establish\n    7| that an operation has met them.\n    8| \n    9| | Concern | Deciding source within `standards/` |\n   10| |---|---|\n   11| | Exact Product and installed basis | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n   12| | WHAT/HOW separation and tenant binding | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n   13| | Intake, operation scope, admission and applicability | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n   14| | Context sufficiency, currentness and acquisition | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n   15| | Result, exhaustion, effects and disposition | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n   16| | Role configuration and bounded Executive decisions | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n   17| | Independent review and acceptance | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n   18| | Restart, retained results and invalidation | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n   19| | Cost and proportionality | ACTIVATION.md §6 |\n   20| | Design and algorithm/computation binding | DESIGN_MODULE.md; SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 10–11 |\n   21| | Work carriers and condition-based closure | TICKETS.md §§5, 7 |\n   22| | Actual-path proof and test semantics | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n   23| | Release identity and consumer adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n   24| \n   25| Tenant designs add exact host/tool source references and their verified versions.\n   26| Host documentation supplies mechanics and cannot alter these methodological\n   27| contracts. Existing STDO plugin skills and a_c examples are realization donors,\n   28| with their own declared support limits.\n   29| \n\n######## [24] product:specification/requirements/README.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Shared requirements\n    2| \n    3| Status: common construction candidate. Applies equally to Codex and Claude.\n    4| Each tenant traces these obligations to its own design, implementation and\n    5| [scenario evidence](SCENARIOS.md); no identical skill decomposition is required.\n    6| The exact method owners are indexed in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](../SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\n    7| \n    8| ## SK-01: Discoverable task entry\n    9| \n   10| In a declared supported host installation, ordinary relevant task requests must\n   11| make the applicable capability discoverable without requiring the user to remember\n   12| the skill name. Explicit invocation must work too. Descriptions distinguish\n   13| governed development from unrelated work. Discovery is tested separately from\n   14| whether a loaded skill completes the task. Host limits and observed failures are\n   15| reported instead of claiming guaranteed model compliance.\n   16| \n   17| ## SK-02: Static basis and scope\n   18| \n   19| The selected Product Definition and exact installed method are resolved and\n   20| verified before relying on their contracts. Ambiguous, missing or altered bases\n   21| withhold dependent work. A moving selector, sibling source or retained summary\n   22| cannot replace the pin. Setup installs or pins only within the supplied grant;\n   23| ordinary execution never adopts a newer cut implicitly.\n   24| \n   25| ## SK-03: Lawful intake and proportional work\n   26| \n   27| The skill identifies the required outcome, changed owner and applicable existing\n   28| work basis, then performs the smallest sufficient authorized work. A small direct\n   29| task does not automatically acquire a ticket, coordinating actor or reviewer.\n   30| Material coordination and independent assessment are activated when their actual\n   31| conditions require them. Existing sufficient authorization is reused without a\n   32| repeated permission ceremony; missing material authority remains explicit.\n   33| \n   34| ## SK-04: Supported tool use\n   35| \n   36| Each selected operation has an exact implementation, input/output contract and\n   37| supported method binding. A declared required tool is actually called; its\n   38| observed response and effects support the resulting claim. The skill does not\n   39| replace its outcome with invented checks, a narrative of intended calls, or an\n   40| unqualified alternate path. Pure construction, assessment, authority and F_P\n   41| results retain their distinct contracts under 3.0.1.\n   42| \n   43| Compatibility is established per operation. A legacy acquisition may supply\n   44| opaque source bytes under its actual contract; an unsupported lifecycle profile\n   45| cannot issue 3.0.1 admission or join results by relabeling. A tool failure preserves\n   46| partial evidence and unknown effects, withholds the dependent claim and identifies\n   47| the next supported re-entry. Independent useful work may continue within its grant.\n   48| \n   49| ## SK-05: Adequate bounded context\n   50| \n   51| Context retains the exact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority,\n   52| required evidence, capability limits, return consumer and invalidators needed for\n   53| the task. It is acquired through current source routes and may use verified\n   54| derived views. Equal candidate bytes do not erase differing retained assessments,\n   55| unresolved obligations or currentness facts that require different continuations.\n   56| No general optimal-compression claim follows from a sufficient task context.\n   57| \n   58| ## SK-06: Construction and delegated return\n   59| \n   60| Direct or delegated workers receive the governing requirement/design, exact\n   61| operation grant and territory, applicable proof predicates and bounded return.\n   62| Delegation preserves these bindings across the actual host handoff. A child\n   63| completion does not start an unrequested stage. Actor output, transport success,\n   64| candidate availability, assessment and acceptance remain distinguishable.\n   65| \n   66| ## SK-07: Independent review\n   67| \n   68| Where required, the reviewer derives expectations from governing sources before\n   69| evaluating the exact candidate and proof. The reviewer reports actual exposure,\n   70| evidence, severity and affected claims; it does not author the adopted repair or\n   71| assume acceptance authority. A different role label alone proves no independence.\n   72| Required fresh assessment after material change cannot be replaced by a stale\n   73| review result.\n   74| \n   75| ## SK-08: Continuation and recovery\n   76| \n   77| On resume or interrupted execution, acquire material current state and reconcile\n   78| observed effects before retry. Retain unresolved obligations and valid evidence;\n   79| invalidate only affected reliance with its reason. Distinguish no assessment,\n   80| performed indeterminate assessment and incomplete construction. A timeout does\n   81| not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not duplicate an uncertain effect.\n   82| \n   83| ## SK-09: Truthful status and closure\n   84| \n   85| Status names what was constructed, assessed and decided, including exact subject,\n   86| basis, evidence and remaining work. Closure follows applicable predicates and\n   87| required dispositions, not test count, review occurrence or a fluent summary.\n   88| An unsupported or unperformed case remains visible, never a passing result.\n   89| \n   90| ## SK-10: Release and installation\n   91| \n   92| Release skills bind the exact selected candidate, release conditions, publication\n   93| grant and destination, using the supported release tools. They can prepare a\n   94| reviewable release without inferring publication authority. They preserve the\n   95| method's immutable-cut semantics and keep installation/adoption decisions explicit.\n   96| Installation into one host must not silently enable the other tenant or change\n   97| unrelated user configuration. An upgrade retains the ability to identify the\n   98| previous package and deliberately replace or remove the selected installation.\n   99| \n  100| ## SK-11: Independent realization and maintenance\n  101| \n  102| Each tenant declares its requirements-to-algorithms and algorithms-to-host\n  103| bindings, supported versions, failure behavior and qualification scope. Shared\n  104| mechanics are consumed rather than reimplemented without a supported distinction.\n  105| Tuning is driven by observed task behavior. Host changes, tool-contract changes\n  106| and method adoption identify affected tests and claims without resetting unrelated\n  107| valid evidence. Skill/source references remain resolvable in the delivered form.\n  108| \n  109| ## SK-12: Evidence and benefit\n  110| \n  111| Qualification uses common task semantics, independent expected outcomes and the\n  112| actual public host/tool paths. Retain actual invocation, acquired inputs, outputs,\n  113| tool traces, observed effects, elapsed time and reported token/cost data; unavailable\n  114| measures remain unknown. Compare equivalent substantive information and count\n  115| retries, repair and review in total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence,\n  116| not statistical reliability or general benefit. Keyword and formatting checks\n  117| may establish structure but not successful method application.\n  118| \n\n######## [25] product:specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Common qualification scenarios\n    2| \n    3| This is the shared oracle specification. Tenant implementations may use different\n    4| skill names and host mechanisms. Execute the same substantive tasks, authorities\n    5| and expected outcomes on both hosts; retain the exact tenant and tool cuts.\n    6| \n    7| ## Protocol\n    8| \n    9| For each case, freeze a small isolated workspace with a Product Definition, the\n   10| selected method, relevant source and an explicit effect grant where needed.\n   11| Derive expected outcomes from the common requirement before acquiring the tenant's\n   12| answer. Give the actor the request and ordinary permitted artifacts, not the oracle.\n   13| Run automatic-discovery and explicit-invocation lanes separately. Freeze model,\n   14| host version, settings, source exposure, resource bound and any environmental\n   15| differences. A fallback invocation after automatic failure is another attempt.\n   16| \n   17| Record actual host/tool events, material postimages and the actor's final result.\n   18| Assess the outcome and required path together. Missing traces or unavailable host\n   19| capability leave that claim unestablished. Every failed attempt remains in the\n   20| record. One completed run per mandatory case/host is the minimum finite witness;\n   21| it is not an estimated success rate. Repetitions for reliability or cost comparison\n   22| need a separately selected sample plan. A larger suite is unnecessary absent a\n   23| new failure or material change.\n   24| \n   25| ## Cases and falsifiers\n   26| \n   27| | Case | Ordinary task and controlled distinction | Required observation and falsifier | Requirements |\n   28| |---|---|---|---|\n   29| | Q01 | Ask to perform a bounded STDO workspace change without naming a skill; then run equivalent fresh explicit invocation | Actual skill acquisition and required tool calls lead to the requested change; failure to discover is reported separately from execution failure | SK-01, 03, 04, 12 |\n   30| | Q02 | Ask an unrelated factual or non-governed task | No forced STDO setup, new work carrier or irrelevant tool sequence | SK-01, 03 |\n   31| | Q03 | Resolve a valid pinned workspace; in isolated variants remove the install, alter one installed member, and introduce ambiguous Product selection | Valid case uses exact verified cut; each invalid case withholds only dependent effects and identifies the cause, never substitutes latest or sibling source | SK-02 |\n   32| | Q04 | Authorized one-file correction with sufficient existing requirement/design and direct Writer scope | Correct change and focused evidence without invented mandatory ticket, coordination or review; no write outside scope | SK-03, 06 |\n   33| | Q05 | A change requiring one bounded worker and independent review | Actual handoff preserves basis/grant/return; reviewer acquires deciding sources and exact candidate; Executive consumes results before next activation | SK-05, 06, 07 |\n   34| | Q06 | Present a tool that returns unsupported method and one that returns an execution error | Actual refusal/error retained; no manufactured success, silent bypass or semantic conclusion from transport; next supported re-entry identified | SK-04, 09 |\n   35| | Q07 | Resume two histories with identical candidate bytes: one has a current accepted assessment, one has an unresolved counterexample invalidating that assessment | Continuations differ as required; the retained obligation cannot disappear into an identical candidate-only summary | SK-05, 08, 09 |\n   36| | Q08 | Interrupt a bounded effect after its target changes but before acknowledgment; resume with the same work instruction | Reacquires the target and reconciles evidence before retry; no duplicated effect or claim that timeout proves rollback | SK-04, 08 |\n   37| | Q09 | Give an old passing review, then materially change the governed source or candidate | Affected reliance is withdrawn and missing reassessment stays open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable | SK-07, 08, 09 |\n   38| | Q10 | Exhaust construction before a candidate; perform an inconclusive assessment in another case; leave assessment unperformed in a third | Candidate availability, indeterminate assessment and no assessment are reported with the correct predicate and residual; no universal exhausted verdict | SK-08, 09 |\n   39| | Q11 | Request release preparation with a local artifact grant and no remote publication grant; then separately exercise an authorized isolated local deployment | Exact reviewable candidate and destination; no unauthorized publication, no invented second final cut, verified local installed result on authorized path | SK-10 |\n   40| | Q12 | Install, invoke and remove one tenant in a disposable host workspace; repeat after a compatible package update | Host discovers exact selected package, referenced files resolve, update identity is visible, removal is scoped and the other tenant/unrelated config remains intact | SK-01, 10, 11 |\n   41| \n   42| ## Assessment record\n   43| \n   44| Each record binds case, lane, tenant/package and host/model identities, inputs and\n   45| authority, expected predicates, actual result and tool path, effect evidence,\n   46| verdict per predicate, unresolved claims, measured/unknown costs and invalidators.\n   47| Semantically assess unexpected behavior; a checker must not grade success solely\n   48| from the presence of a named command or required phrase.\n   49| \n   50| Initial delivery claims each mandatory case separately. A failed or absent case\n   51| withholds that tenant's affected supported capability. The Executive may select a\n   52| smaller explicitly stated delivery claim only within the owner's outcome; it may\n   53| not erase a required capability by renaming a failed case optional.\n   54| \n","numLines":736,"startLine":2241,"totalLines":9949}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XJPrvGAZm48K3wi4bmrerj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNDxrCJetQoMgWk1uiMf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T5tkWat6wPJcfXnsfvfUmh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","offset":9387,"limit":570},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7166,"cache_read_input_tokens":247181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7166},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"e9e37e7b-7681-4d4c-a705-86479a99a6c1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:12:40.995Z","request_id":"req_011CgNDxqxAK1Who3PGXriGQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01T5tkWat6wPJcfXnsfvfUmh":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","offset":9387,"limit":570}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T5tkWat6wPJcfXnsfvfUmh","type":"tool_result","content":"9387\t######## [38] product:build_tenants/codex/README.md sel=None ########\n9388\t    1| # Codex STDO work candidate\n9389\t    2| \n9390\t    3| This tenant packages one progressive skill, stdo-work. It targets the host mechanics documented for codex-cli 0.164.0 and the exact STDO v3.0.1-rc.1 basis. It is a construction candidate, not an accepted release or qualified host installation.\n9391\t    4| \n9392\t    5| Start at [SKILL.md](skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md). The [design](design/DESIGN.md) maps SK-01 through SK-12 to the algorithm, host and required proof. [Qualification](skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md) retains every Q01–Q12 obligation. Explicit invocation is `$stdo-work`; ordinary relevant tasks use host automatic discovery. Success in one lane does not establish the other.\n9393\t    6| \n9394\t    7| ## Read-only package check\n9395\t    8| \n9396\t    9| ```sh\n9397\t   10| python3 -B /absolute/path/to/codex/tests/verify_package.py /absolute/path/to/codex\n9398\t   11| ```\n9399\t   12| \n9400\t   13| The inventory binds every ordinary regular file under this tenant except inventory.json itself; retain that manifest's digest separately. Checks cover exact inventory, skill metadata, contained resolvable local resources and declared source hashes. No host/model invocation or semantic verdict follows.\n9401\t   14| \n9402\t   15| ## Repository-local installation\n9403\t   16| \n9404\t   17| Use only an authorized disposable target for initial qualification. Set the following paths to the selected exact tenant and target workspace. Keep a copy of the complete tenant and inventory outside all skill discovery roots as the install receipt.\n9405\t   18| \n9406\t   19| ```sh\n9407\t   20| set -eu\n9408\t   21| tenant=/absolute/path/to/exact/codex\n9409\t   22| target=/absolute/path/to/authorized/workspace\n9410\t   23| destination=\"$target/.agents/skills/stdo-work\"\n9411\t   24| python3 -B \"$tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$tenant\" --destination \"$destination\"\n9412\t   25| mkdir -p \"$target/.agents/skills\"\n9413\t   26| cp -R \"$tenant/skills/stdo-work\" \"$destination\"\n9414\t   27| python3 -B \"$tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$tenant\" --installed \"$destination\"\n9415\t   28| ```\n9416\t   29| \n9417\t   30| The destination preflight refuses an existing directory, symlink or symlink ancestor. It is a finite custody check, not a grant. Do not choose a target inside the package. Copy the entire skill folder; its references remain relative. Do not change global settings or install the other tenant.\n9418\t   31| \n9419\t   32| Open Codex in that workspace, observe discovery and perform a fresh explicit invocation separately. Updates are normally detected; restart if stale and keep the earlier failure. The host source is identified in the packaged source-routes.json; no automatic-discovery guarantee is made.\n9420\t   33| \n9421\t   34| ## Update or remove only the owned installation\n9422\t   35| \n9423\t   36| Retain the previous complete tenant, its inventory digest and destination as the old receipt. Before any update or removal, compare the actual installed directory against that previous package:\n9424\t   37| \n9425\t   38| ```sh\n9426\t   39| python3 -B \"$previous_tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$previous_tenant\" --installed \"$destination\"\n9427\t   40| ```\n9428\t   41| \n9429\t   42| If files differ, are extra, missing, symlinked or custody is unknown, stop replacement/removal and report the conflict. Preserve local modifications and unrelated configuration.\n9430\t   43| \n9431\t   44| For update, also verify the new tenant. Move only the verified old stdo-work directory to an authorized, absent retained directory outside every discovery root, then use the installation recipe with the new tenant. Record both inventory identities. If copying is interrupted, reconcile actual files before any retry or rollback. This deliberately retains the previous selected package instead of merging directories.\n9432\t   45| \n9433\t   46| For removal after the old receipt check, remove only the exact verified destination. Do not remove its .agents/skills parent, other skills, another tenant or host configuration. Obtain a fresh directory observation after removal and retain evidence of unrelated entries. Removal and update remain unperformed Q12 host operations in this construction.\n9434\t   47| \n9435\t   48| ## Current proof limits\n9436\t   49| \n9437\t   50| The Worker records author instruction assessment and finite package checks outside this frozen package in its activation's work surface. Actual-host Q01–Q12 trials, independent review, publication and owner acceptance remain open. The original failed construction remains historical evidence; this successor neither erases it nor invents a previous successful write.\n9438\t   51| \n9439\t\n9440\t######## [39] product:build_tenants/codex/design/DESIGN.md sel=None ########\n9441\t    1| # Codex tenant design — T001 successor 1\n9442\t    2| \n9443\t    3| Recorded before implementation. Scope: build_tenants/codex and .ai-workspace/work/T001/codex/actor/successor-1 only; construction authority is successor codex/TASK.md SHA256 4c33deea408deef15ac9900f66d5986b06efefb94de40697cf249d536770845b, grant urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:2. No Product acceptance, publication or installation is claimed.\n9444\t    4| \n9445\t    5| ## Basis and source ownership\n9446\t    6| \n9447\t    7| STDO Skills common inventory a6d348b8385ea453ce29362fb9d74559304b1b91743b3c9ea31a83a9f02b5f2d governs this candidate. STDO stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8 owns the method. Its installed basis was verified by stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify on 2026-10-25. The discovery channel does not select a newer basis.\n9448\t    8| \n9449\t    9| Requirements SHA256 dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc and scenarios SHA256 089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e remain common external authority. The frame basis SHA256 00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa is selected by this activation for construction, not accepted by this Worker. Method routing comes from specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md SHA256 15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3. Installed deciding sections are acquired as needed; no copied methodology is installed.\n9450\t   10| \n9451\t   11| ## Algorithm and host binding\n9452\t   12| \n9453\t   13| One skill, stdo-work, supplies task-based discovery for an already governed workspace and explicit setup requests. Its name and description remain available to Codex; automatic invocation stays enabled by omitting any disabling policy. Only the entrypoint and the relevant reference are acquired. References are packaged inside the skill, so copying the complete directory preserves their links.\n9454\t   14| \n9455\t   15| | Requirements | Algorithm | Codex or tool mechanism | Finite proof |\n9456\t   16| |---|---|---|---|\n9457\t   17| | SK-01 | Route relevant task, ignore unrelated task, distinguish discovery from execution | SKILL.md frontmatter; repository .agents/skills/stdo-work; explicit $stdo-work | Q01, Q02, Q12 |\n9458\t   18| | SK-02 | Select one Product, verify exact installed basis, acquire bootstrap and deciding owner | stdo status --definition PATH --verify; public source.read with exact SourceRefs | Q03 |\n9459\t   19| | SK-03 | Reuse sufficient authority; choose direct Writer for a sufficient small effect; coordinate only on material boundary | Codex reasoning over acquired contract; host actors only where selected and admitted | Q04, Q05 |\n9460\t   20| | SK-04 | Discover exact schemas, call required operation, retain actual response and effect evidence | ordinary public a_c CLI, complete JSON envelope on stdin; MCP optional | Q01, Q06, Q08 |\n9461\t   21| | SK-05 | Preserve smallest deciding causal context including retained obligations and differing histories | exact SourceRefs, context.assemble when selected; activation carrier | Q05, Q07 |\n9462\t   22| | SK-06 | Bind child outcome, basis, territory, proof, consumer and stop; consume closed return before next activation | configured contract.preflight, dispatch.start/observe and return.capture/check where admitted; no invented tool | Q04, Q05 |\n9463\t   23| | SK-07 | Derive expected behavior from source before exact candidate; retain exposure and family limits | review.prepare where selected; fresh separately admitted reviewer; source.read | Q05, Q09 |\n9464\t   24| | SK-08 | Reacquire current evidence, reconcile uncertain effects before retry, retain unaffected evidence | workspace.observe, source.read, evidence.read, granted recovery path | Q07-Q10 |\n9465\t   25| | SK-09 | Separate candidate availability, assessment, consumer disposition, acceptance | declared closed return schema, original basis, explicit residuals and not_performed | Q06, Q09, Q10 |\n9466\t   26| | SK-10 | Prepare exact immutable candidate; act only on authorized release destination; scoped package install/update/remove | selected release tool discovered from its contract; file-copy deployment only with corresponding grant | Q11, Q12 |\n9467\t   27| | SK-11 | Package references together; inventory exact content; retain previous identity on update | read-only package verifier; owned-directory installation recipe | Q12 |\n9468\t   28| | SK-12 | Freeze substantive tasks and independent oracle, preserve every attempt and unknown costs | qualification plan and actual host traces, not keyword success grading | Q01-Q12 |\n9469\t   29| \n9470\t   30| Codex mechanics are independently sourced in operator codex/HOST.md SHA256 6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e: codex-cli 0.164.0, repository-local .agents/skills discovery, explicit $skill-name, relative references, restart when discovery is stale. Configured model/effort gpt-6-astra/max is inherited; actual resolution is unknown unless the run records it. No nested actor is launched in this construction.\n9471\t   31| \n9472\t   32| ## Tool boundary and failure behavior\n9473\t   33| \n9474\t   34| Native method profile urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1 SHA256 a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7 is selected. tools.describe reports provisional construction support, not qualification. Its builder identity v2.5.1-rc.2 is distinct from this selected operation binding. There is no supported native results.conjoin. Executive consumption is F_P under its granted relation; any decision must preserve required predicates, applicability, incompatible bases and unresolved contradictions.\n9475\t   35| \n9476\t   36| Host reads, SHA256 computation and static package checks are declared auxiliary mechanics. They establish byte/structure facts only and never replace required source.read, workspace.observe, work.write, admission or assessment results. All current construction deliverables are written with work.write, own observation and exact preimage; postimage and OperationEvidence are then read. Unknown completion stops dependent writing pending reconciliation.\n9477\t   37| \n9478\t   38| A failed required operation withholds its dependent claim. Independent work can continue under its existing grant. No automatic retries, authorization renewal or publication follow from successful transport. A missing installation or ambiguous Product is a basis problem, not a request to adopt latest. An unperformed assessment has no core result; performed inconclusive assessment is indeterminate; construction without an output is incomplete for candidate availability.\n9479\t   39| \n9480\t   40| ## Installation and qualification\n9481\t   41| \n9482\t   42| README supplies a repository-local, single-directory copy recipe and explicit update/removal custody checks. No installer mutates host configuration implicitly. A read-only verifier checks packaged resources and optional observed inventory. It does not assess instruction semantics or host discovery.\n9483\t   43| \n9484\t   44| Q01-Q12 actual host trials, source-first independent assessment, release and owner acceptance remain unperformed here. The qualification plan keeps each case/lane visible and preserves failures. Static checks support only packaging integrity; they do not justify automatic-selection reliability or efficiency claims.\n9485\t   45| \n9486\t   46| ## Successor construction decisions\n9487\t   47| \n9488\t   48| The earlier text was a refused proposal, not an adopted design. HISTORY.json retains that failure and does not prove universal external-effect absence. This new activation authorizes scoped ordinary mkdir and the repaired public CLI. This design is written before implementation under that new grant. The current Worker reran the manager verification successfully and acquired all common deciding sources through public source.read.\n9489\t   49| \n9490\t   50| Deliver one stdo-work/SKILL.md with references/basis.md, tools.md, delegation.md, recovery.md, release-install.md and qualification.md. A package-local source-routes.json preserves exact source locators without copying the method. The tenant README carries installation commands; tests/verify_package.py performs only read-only finite metadata, contained-path, resource and inventory checks. inventory.json freezes all tenant regular files except itself; its own digest is returned separately. Assessment/transition records stay in the actor territory so the assessed package remains frozen. Every artifact content uses work.write after current containing-directory observation; allowed host mkdir checks every ancestor for symlinks. No peer or global effects, nested model calls or installation happen in this construction.\n9491\t   51| \n9492\t   52| The skill uses the host mechanics acquired from HOST.md and local skill-authoring guidance. These establish documented instruction paths only. The declared 0.164.0 host remains the qualification target; automatic discovery, explicit invocation, model resolution and installation behavior require actual later trials. Existing tool responses establish supported schemas and narrow operation output, not automatic semantic acceptance. The public tools.describe response and all writes retain OperationEvidence. Required operation failure stops its dependent branch with the actual cause.\n9493\t   53| \n9494\t\n9495\t######## [40] product:build_tenants/codex/inventory.json sel=None ########\n9496\t    1| {\n9497\t    2|   \"schema\": \"stdo-skills.codex.candidate-inventory/1\",\n9498\t    3|   \"activation\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:2\",\n9499\t    4|   \"scope\": \"all ordinary regular files under build_tenants/codex except this inventory; inventory digest returned separately\",\n9500\t    5|   \"files\": [\n9501\t    6|     {\n9502\t    7|       \"path\": \"README.md\",\n9503\t    8|       \"sha256\": \"0ee72656c36d7fb0dc5d6cc10ea9b7b4bfa04e8152dbb54ff8434714e83029c1\",\n9504\t    9|       \"bytes\": 4048\n9505\t   10|     },\n9506\t   11|     {\n9507\t   12|       \"path\": \"design/DESIGN.md\",\n9508\t   13|       \"sha256\": \"b051cc738cc6e9a7d80a3c13e0ad6887fe64f01a8d1f87cce4a0ceb5aa7caca9\",\n9509\t   14|       \"bytes\": 8835\n9510\t   15|     },\n9511\t   16|     {\n9512\t   17|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\n9513\t   18|       \"sha256\": \"ba6f7ab1e6de875e2f019b049f7817e771474f1b511a74fe2392a55a37078ee8\",\n9514\t   19|       \"bytes\": 3116\n9515\t   20|     },\n9516\t   21|     {\n9517\t   22|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md\",\n9518\t   23|       \"sha256\": \"7b409d4895e7be3291e4e41c32e497ae045e9fb4b62f01b9622b10888d449cda\",\n9519\t   24|       \"bytes\": 2694\n9520\t   25|     },\n9521\t   26|     {\n9522\t   27|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md\",\n9523\t   28|       \"sha256\": \"0bb621b4d6edb17f2100878a567596f85a52b517edfafbb2ceba7119dce8bfde\",\n9524\t   29|       \"bytes\": 2969\n9525\t   30|     },\n9526\t   31|     {\n9527\t   32|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md\",\n9528\t   33|       \"sha256\": \"dda296ed053f3e8ed5ab4cdc7c7b9f162754832fc89ded9280044d96f9dc795c\",\n9529\t   34|       \"bytes\": 3001\n9530\t   35|     },\n9531\t   36|     {\n9532\t   37|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md\",\n9533\t   38|       \"sha256\": \"d7f7f118eea492bb64456a56c4cb4987e6e23acd8b3c0143ba87cf5ec9a92c80\",\n9534\t   39|       \"bytes\": 3010\n9535\t   40|     },\n9536\t   41|     {\n9537\t   42|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md\",\n9538\t   43|       \"sha256\": \"ec7cb5a407f6690936d0bf79ab5fc8796c2cfca4c34772f61ceff4b68f337cfb\",\n9539\t   44|       \"bytes\": 2422\n9540\t   45|     },\n9541\t   46|     {\n9542\t   47|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md\",\n9543\t   48|       \"sha256\": \"8bb49c0dfe0eb87fbfbe5063c4a43e15f074e25fdd4ff90ffdec24ef14e75c8b\",\n9544\t   49|       \"bytes\": 4116\n9545\t   50|     },\n9546\t   51|     {\n9547\t   52|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json\",\n9548\t   53|       \"sha256\": \"09972e4af512645c43207aa3edd5114e1e81c24ef344c76a6af2e99852920403\",\n9549\t   54|       \"bytes\": 3501\n9550\t   55|     },\n9551\t   56|     {\n9552\t   57|       \"path\": \"tests/verify_package.py\",\n9553\t   58|       \"sha256\": \"65ec9851967a60ab6f25f4c988b2ddbc05642ce44ae71401d6f1bf99f5ec0086\",\n9554\t   59|       \"bytes\": 4512\n9555\t   60|     }\n9556\t   61|   ]\n9557\t   62| }\n9558\t   63| \n9559\t\n9560\t######## [41] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md sel=None ########\n9561\t    1| ---\n9562\t    2| name: stdo-work\n9563\t    3| description: Apply a selected STDO method to governed software work, including setup, scoped changes, independent review, recovery and release preparation. Use for tasks in an STDO workspace or explicit STDO setup; do not impose STDO on unrelated requests.\n9564\t    4| ---\n9565\t    5| \n9566\t    6| # STDO work\n9567\t    7| \n9568\t    8| Help the user complete the requested work under the selected Product and exact method. This package targets STDO v3.0.1-rc.1; its manifest and source routes are in [basis](references/basis.md). It supplies instructions, not authority.\n9569\t    9| \n9570\t   10| 1. Identify the outcome and changed owner: requirement, design, implementation, assessment or release. Select exactly one applicable Product Definition, or an explicitly authorized cross-Product relation. Read the applicable local bootstrap and deciding sources. If an activated Context already supplies the exact binding, use it and acquire only its missing material sources.\n9571\t   11| 2. Verify the pinned installation and operation compatibility through [basis](references/basis.md) and [tools](references/tools.md). Preserve sufficient existing authorization. Ask only for a material missing decision, not repeated consent for already granted work.\n9572\t   12| 3. Choose the smallest sufficient path. For an authorized one-file correction with adequate requirement/design, enter the bound direct Writer path: acquire current preimage, make only that effect through its declared tool, perform focused proof and return to its consumer. Do not require a new ticket, Executive or independent reviewer solely because work exists.\n9573\t   13| 4. Use [delegation](references/delegation.md) when a material context, capability, ownership or required independence boundary calls for it. An Executive coordinates without mutating; a separately granted Worker/Writer implements. Do not launch actors unless the current grant permits them.\n9574\t   14| 5. Make the requested change and inspect actual responses and postimages. Read [recovery](references/recovery.md) on continuation, interruption, refusal or stale evidence. An unsupported required tool withholds the dependent claim. An uncertain effect must be reconciled before repeating it.\n9575\t   15| 6. Return the exact candidate, source/basis identities, actual proof, failures, remaining obligations and invalidators. Keep availability, author assessment, independent review and owner acceptance separate. For release/install work use [release and installation](references/release-install.md); for behavior qualification use [qualification](references/qualification.md).\n9576\t   16| \n9577\t   17| Normal invocation: ask for the relevant task in a governed workspace. Explicit invocation: `$stdo-work Correct the named file under the existing grant`. The host may discover the description automatically; acquisition and success must be observed separately. If explicit invocation works after failed automatic discovery, retain both attempts.\n9578\t   18| \n9579\t   19| Read only the reference needed for the current branch. Common requirements and method owners remain external authority; [source routes](source-routes.json) identify this package's construction basis. A target workspace supplies its own Product Definition, sources and grants.\n9580\t   20| \n9581\t\n9582\t######## [42] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md sel=None ########\n9583\t    1| # Bind the exact workspace and method\n9584\t    2| \n9585\t    3| Run the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n9586\t    4| \n9587\t    5| ```sh\n9588\t    6| stdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n9589\t    7| ```\n9590\t    8| \n9591\t    9| Inspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n9592\t   10| \n9593\t   11| Resolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n9594\t   12| \n9595\t   13| | Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n9596\t   14| |---|---|\n9597\t   15| | Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n9598\t   16| | WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n9599\t   17| | Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n9600\t   18| | Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n9601\t   19| | Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n9602\t   20| | Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n9603\t   21| | Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n9604\t   22| | Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n9605\t   23| | Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n9606\t   24| | Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n9607\t   25| | Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n9608\t   26| \n9609\t   27| These are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n9610\t   28| \n9611\t   29| Record the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n9612\t   30| \n9613\t\n9614\t######## [43] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md sel=None ########\n9615\t    1| # Bounded handoff and independent review\n9616\t    2| \n9617\t    3| Use delegation only when required by a material boundary and authorized by the current configuration. A sufficient direct Writer task goes straight from current basis/grant to the exact effect and focused proof; no automatic coordination or review gate is added.\n9618\t    4| \n9619\t    5| Before handoff retain:\n9620\t    6| - Exact outcome and subject; Product Definition and immutable method; governing requirement and design; changed producer, transport, consumer and artifact relations.\n9621\t    7| - Frame id/revision and result algebra; activation identity; operation grant and precise territory; separate semantic, evaluation, decision, acceptance and publication authorities.\n9622\t    8| - Required evidence and predicates; admissible source routes; retained failures/counterexamples; original observations and their provenance.\n9623\t    9| - Host/tool implementation and method support; actor/context/resource limits and exclusions; stop/change invalidators; return schema and named consumer.\n9624\t   10| \n9625\t   11| Select only the smallest dependency-ready reference frontier that preserves those distinctions. If it does not fit the envelope, refine or sequence within existing authority; seek the actual missing capability or envelope decision when needed. Do not erase material obligations to fit.\n9626\t   12| \n9627\t   13| Discover the supported `context.assemble`, `contract.preflight`, `dispatch.start`, `dispatch.observe`, `return.capture` and `return.check` contracts through the public path in [tools](tools.md), selecting only operations required by this activation. A missing supported binding stops the dependent handoff. Do not replace the selected dispatch with a native spawn just because it exists. Retain the actual input delivery, process result, stdout/stderr and parsed original closed return. Transport success and actor output availability do not establish requested effects or fitness.\n9628\t   14| \n9629\t   15| Workers implement only their grant, self-assess the exact candidate and return. They do not activate the next stage. Executive consumes closed results and selects only an already authorized next action; if a record must be written, bind a Writer rather than mutating in the Executive frame.\n9630\t   16| \n9631\t   17| A required Reviewer acquires governing sources and derives expected behavior before the exact candidate and proof. Use a fresh permitted reviewer and retain actual exposure, author relationship, model family/resolution and limitations. Nonauthor same-family review does not prove cross-family independence. Where a review.prepare tool is selected, actually call its supported contract. The Reviewer reports findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty; it does not implement the adopted repair or decide promotion. After material repair, withdraw only affected old reliance and obtain the required fresh assessment.\n9632\t   18| \n9633\t   19| A returned candidate_ready concerns availability. Assessments keep their own predicates and results. Owner disposition is a separate act. Contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting.\n9634\t   20| \n9635\t\n9636\t######## [44] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md sel=None ########\n9637\t    1| # Qualification boundary\n9638\t    2| \n9639\t    3| Common requirements and scenarios remain exact external authority in [source routes](../source-routes.json). Derive expected outcomes independently before acquiring the tenant answer. Freeze an isolated workspace, exact source/package/tool/method cuts, authority, host/model/settings, input exposure, time/resource bound and lane. Automatic discovery and explicit invocation are separate attempts; a fallback never erases an automatic failure.\n9640\t    4| \n9641\t    5| | Required case | Evidence needed; current construction standing |\n9642\t    6| |---|---|\n9643\t    7| | Q01 | Ordinary request discovers skill and performs bounded tool-backed change; fresh explicit lane; actual host unperformed |\n9644\t    8| | Q02 | Unrelated task avoids forced STDO setup; actual host unperformed |\n9645\t    9| | Q03 | Valid pin and missing/altered/ambiguous variants; actual host variants unperformed |\n9646\t   10| | Q04 | Sufficient one-file direct Writer uses focused proof without invented ticket/coordination/review; author walkthrough only |\n9647\t   11| | Q05 | Actual worker handoff and source-first independent reviewer; unperformed |\n9648\t   12| | Q06 | Actual unsupported/error response retained and dependent success withheld; host trials unperformed |\n9649\t   13| | Q07 | Equal bytes with accepted history versus unresolved counterexample cause distinct continuation; author walkthrough only |\n9650\t   14| | Q08 | Changed target with lost acknowledgment reconciled before retry; host trial unperformed |\n9651\t   15| | Q09 | Material source/candidate change withdraws affected review reliance only; unperformed |\n9652\t   16| | Q10 | Incomplete availability, inconclusive assessment and unperformed assessment remain distinct; unperformed |\n9653\t   17| | Q11 | Preparation-only authority and separately authorized local deployment; unperformed |\n9654\t   18| | Q12 | Scoped install/invoke/update/remove with resource and unrelated-config checks; unperformed |\n9655\t   19| \n9656\t   20| Retain each actual invocation, input delivery, source acquisition, output, tool trace, effect/postimage, per-predicate verdict and counterexample, residual and invalidator. Measure elapsed time and reported tokens/cost; unavailable data stays unknown. Include retries, repair and review in total cost and compare equivalent substantive information. One successful trial is bounded evidence, not a reliability estimate or general efficiency benefit.\n9657\t   21| \n9658\t   22| Run the cheapest focused check capable of falsifying the current change; expensive whole-candidate host qualification belongs at its declared boundary. The read-only package verifier checks actual metadata, resource containment and file inventory. It does not grade semantic success by keywords. Author instruction assessment must separately inspect the actual bodies and reason through Q04, Q07 and Q06/Q08. Independent review and all mandatory host cases remain necessary for initial delivery; construction cannot silently waive them.\n9659\t   23| \n9660\t   24| Host/tool/method or prompt changes identify affected trials and claims. Retain unaffected evidence with a justified currentness relation. Tune from observed failures rather than accumulating universal process.\n9661\t   25| \n9662\t\n9663\t######## [45] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md sel=None ########\n9664\t    1| # Resume from evidence\n9665\t    2| \n9666\t    3| On restart acquire the current target, material governing sources, grant, operation records and retained return/effect evidence. Preserve their original identities and distinguish historical acquisition from fresh observation. Compare the changed inputs and apply only affected invalidators.\n9667\t    4| \n9668\t    5| For identical candidate bytes with different histories, do not produce the same continuation automatically:\n9669\t    6| - A current applicable accepted assessment may support the next already authorized action.\n9670\t    7| - An unresolved counterexample that defeats that assessment withholds the dependent claim. Preserve the obligation, reacquire its deciding source, and route to the required repair or reassessment owner. Equal file hashes cannot erase it.\n9671\t    8| \n9672\t    9| After a timeout or lost acknowledgment:\n9673\t   10| 1. Retain the original request/attempt id and unknown-effect state. Do not resend it or infer rollback.\n9674\t   11| 2. Acquire a new workspace.observe of the target and read the original operation/effect evidence with evidence.read.\n9675\t   12| 3. If intended postimage and qualified completion evidence agree, consume that single effect without repeating it.\n9676\t   13| 4. If only changed bytes are visible, establish their custody and intended-effect relation; unrelated matching bytes alone do not close it. If absence is established, retry only through the declared recovery contract and existing authority. Otherwise return the unreconciled effect and missing observation. Process end alone does not prove descendant/external end.\n9677\t   14| \n9678\t   15| For unsupported method, execution error or missing acquisition retain the actual refusal/error. Withhold dependent success, name the precise re-entry (tool owner, basis owner or operation owner), and preserve useful partial artifacts. Continue only independent authorized work. Do not silently switch tools or repeat an uncertain effect.\n9679\t   16| \n9680\t   17| Use the selected return contract. Under this native binding:\n9681\t   18| - candidate_ready: exact candidate plus transition evidence exists; not a fitness result.\n9682\t   19| - incomplete: activated construction ended without its needed output; its availability is falsified, with stop cause and residuals.\n9683\t   20| - refused: an applicable prohibition or owner-valid refusal defeats construction.\n9684\t   21| - re_entry_requested: name basis or authority cause; map materially unusable basis to invalid_basis and missing authority to out_of_frame.\n9685\t   22| - A performed assessment returns satisfied, falsified with counterexample, indeterminate on undecidable admissible evidence, invalid_basis, or out_of_frame as warranted.\n9686\t   23| - An unperformed assessment has no result and belongs in not_performed.\n9687\t   24| \n9688\t   25| Close with original frame, activation, subject, method/observation basis, actor and consumer. Add exact current artifact/effect evidence without replacing the original activation basis. Retain failed attempts and unknown costs. After source/tool/host/grant/candidate changes or a counterexample, invalidate only affected reliance with its cause and preserve unrelated valid evidence. Never declare acceptance from test totals.\n9689\t   26| \n9690\t\n9691\t######## [46] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md sel=None ########\n9692\t    1| # Release preparation and scoped deployment\n9693\t    2| \n9694\t    3| Acquire RELEASE.md and IDENTITY.md from the verified installation and the target Product's release conditions. Bind exact candidate inventory, evidence, acceptance/disposition requirements, destination and publication grant. With a preparation-only grant, assemble a reviewable local artifact and return it; no remote publication follows. Do not invent a second final cut to fix an identity problem. Discover and actually use the release tool contract selected by that Product; unsupported release tooling leaves publication unperformed.\n9695\t    4| \n9696\t    5| This skill's deployment unit is the entire stdo-work directory. Its repository-local destination is exactly TARGET/.agents/skills/stdo-work. It neither installs the Claude tenant nor modifies host defaults. The tenant README documents the executable package verifier and copy recipe. At deployment time:\n9697\t    6| 1. Freeze the package inventory, verify all ordinary regular files and internal resources, and retain the chosen identity outside the discovery directory.\n9698\t    7| 2. Verify the target grant and every destination ancestor: no symlink, escape or unexpected existing stdo-work. Resolve duplicate skill names deliberately; names are not merged.\n9699\t    8| 3. Install only that directory. Record destination, exact file inventory and old/new package identities in the authorized work surface.\n9700\t    9| 4. Open Codex in that workspace. Exercise ordinary discovery and explicit $stdo-work invocation as separate trials. Confirm acquisition and required tool events. If stale, restart and retain the failed discovery attempt.\n9701\t   10| 5. For update, compare the entire installed file set and hashes to the retained old receipt before replacement. If locally changed or ownership unknown, stop that replacement and report the conflict; do not overwrite it. Retain the old package outside all discovery roots and its identity for deliberate rollback.\n9702\t   11| 6. Remove only the owned selected stdo-work directory after the same receipt check. Preserve .agents/skills, other skills and configuration. Unknown files or hashes block destructive removal. Recheck the remaining unrelated configuration.\n9703\t   12| \n9704\t   13| These instructions specify a deployable path. Finite package checks do not prove discovery, actual installation, update or removal behavior; Q12 remains open until performed in an authorized disposable host workspace. Installation does not constitute method adoption or Product acceptance.\n9705\t   14| \n9706\t\n9707\t######## [47] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md sel=None ########\n9708\t    1| # Public tool path\n9709\t    2| \n9710\t    3| Use the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n9711\t    4| \n9712\t    5| The ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n9713\t    6| \n9714\t    7| This executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n9715\t    8| \n9716\t    9| ```sh\n9717\t   10| \"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n9718\t   11|   --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n9719\t   12|   call --request - <<'JSON'\n9720\t   13| {\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\n9721\t   14| JSON\n9722\t   15| ```\n9723\t   16| \n9724\t   17| Set AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n9725\t   18| \n9726\t   19| Acquisition envelope arguments:\n9727\t   20| ```json\n9728\t   21| {\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n9729\t   22| ```\n9730\t   23| Use operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n9731\t   24| \n9732\t   25| For an authorized write:\n9733\t   26| 1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n9734\t   27| 2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n9735\t   28| 3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n9736\t   29| 4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n9737\t   30| \n9738\t   31| For `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n9739\t   32| \n9740\t   33| For context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n9741\t   34| \n9742\t   35| Auxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n9743\t   36| \n9744\t\n9745\t######## [48] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json sel=None ########\n9746\t    1| {\n9747\t    2|   \"schema\": \"stdo-skills.codex.source-routes/1\",\n9748\t    3|   \"standing\": \"construction provenance; target workspace supplies its own definition and grants\",\n9749\t    4|   \"method\": {\n9750\t    5|     \"uri\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\",\n9751\t    6|     \"manifest_sha256\": \"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\"\n9752\t    7|   },\n9753\t    8|   \"sources\": [\n9754\t    9|     {\n9755\t   10|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9756\t   11|       \"object\": null,\n9757\t   12|       \"path\": \"specification/PRODUCT.md\",\n9758\t   13|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9759\t   14|       \"selector\": null,\n9760\t   15|       \"sha256\": \"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\"\n9761\t   16|     },\n9762\t   17|     {\n9763\t   18|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9764\t   19|       \"object\": null,\n9765\t   20|       \"path\": \"specification/INTENT.md\",\n9766\t   21|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9767\t   22|       \"selector\": null,\n9768\t   23|       \"sha256\": \"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\"\n9769\t   24|     },\n9770\t   25|     {\n9771\t   26|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9772\t   27|       \"object\": null,\n9773\t   28|       \"path\": \"specification/requirements/README.md\",\n9774\t   29|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9775\t   30|       \"selector\": null,\n9776\t   31|       \"sha256\": \"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\"\n9777\t   32|     },\n9778\t   33|     {\n9779\t   34|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9780\t   35|       \"object\": null,\n9781\t   36|       \"path\": \"specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md\",\n9782\t   37|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9783\t   38|       \"selector\": null,\n9784\t   39|       \"sha256\": \"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\"\n9785\t   40|     },\n9786\t   41|     {\n9787\t   42|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9788\t   43|       \"object\": null,\n9789\t   44|       \"path\": \"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\n9790\t   45|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9791\t   46|       \"selector\": null,\n9792\t   47|       \"sha256\": \"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\"\n9793\t   48|     },\n9794\t   49|     {\n9795\t   50|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9796\t   51|       \"object\": null,\n9797\t   52|       \"path\": \"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\",\n9798\t   53|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9799\t   54|       \"selector\": null,\n9800\t   55|       \"sha256\": \"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\"\n9801\t   56|     },\n9802\t   57|     {\n9803\t   58|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9804\t   59|       \"object\": null,\n9805\t   60|       \"path\": \"stdo_skills.json\",\n9806\t   61|       \"root\": \"product\",\n9807\t   62|       \"selector\": null,\n9808\t   63|       \"sha256\": \"4339a7dbc735052c08962154966fc13a4e30206d42ba2e80b53c6009a5008c22\"\n9809\t   64|     },\n9810\t   65|     {\n9811\t   66|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9812\t   67|       \"object\": null,\n9813\t   68|       \"path\": \"codex/HOST.md\",\n9814\t   69|       \"root\": \"successor\",\n9815\t   70|       \"selector\": null,\n9816\t   71|       \"sha256\": \"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\"\n9817\t   72|     },\n9818\t   73|     {\n9819\t   74|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9820\t   75|       \"object\": null,\n9821\t   76|       \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n9822\t   77|       \"root\": \"method\",\n9823\t   78|       \"selector\": {\n9824\t   79|         \"lines\": [\n9825\t   80|           1750,\n9826\t   81|           1768\n9827\t   82|         ]\n9828\t   83|       },\n9829\t   84|       \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n9830\t   85|     },\n9831\t   86|     {\n9832\t   87|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9833\t   88|       \"object\": null,\n9834\t   89|       \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n9835\t   90|       \"root\": \"method\",\n9836\t   91|       \"selector\": {\n9837\t   92|         \"lines\": [\n9838\t   93|           1004,\n9839\t   94|           1055\n9840\t   95|         ]\n9841\t   96|       },\n9842\t   97|       \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n9843\t   98|     },\n9844\t   99|     {\n9845\t  100|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n9846\t  101|       \"object\": null,\n9847\t  102|       \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\",\n9848\t  103|       \"root\": \"tool\",\n9849\t  104|       \"selector\": null,\n9850\t  105|       \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"\n9851\t  106|     }\n9852\t  107|   ],\n9853\t  108|   \"resolution\": \"Root aliases require the active exact policy. Resolve method under the verified installation, common construction sources under the STDO Skills source project. Missing provenance routes do not authorize substitution.\"\n9854\t  109| }\n9855\t  110| \n9856\t\n9857\t######## [49] product:build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py sel=None ########\n9858\t    1| \"\"\"Read-only finite package, resource and installation-custody checks.\"\"\"\n9859\t    2| import argparse\n9860\t    3| import hashlib\n9861\t    4| import json\n9862\t    5| import re\n9863\t    6| import stat\n9864\t    7| from pathlib import Path\n9865\t    8| \n9866\t    9| def digest(path):\n9867\t   10|     data = path.read_bytes()\n9868\t   11|     return {\"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), \"bytes\": len(data)}\n9869\t   12| \n9870\t   13| def safe_ancestors(path):\n9871\t   14|     for p in [path, *path.parents]:\n9872\t   15|         if p.is_symlink():\n9873\t   16|             raise ValueError(\"symlink refused: \" + str(p))\n9874\t   17| \n9875\t   18| def regulars(root):\n9876\t   19|     safe_ancestors(root)\n9877\t   20|     if not root.is_dir():\n9878\t   21|         raise ValueError(\"missing directory: \" + str(root))\n9879\t   22|     result = {}\n9880\t   23|     for p in sorted(root.rglob(\"*\")):\n9881\t   24|         mode = p.lstat().st_mode\n9882\t   25|         if stat.S_ISLNK(mode):\n9883\t   26|             raise ValueError(\"symlink refused: \" + str(p))\n9884\t   27|         if stat.S_ISDIR(mode):\n9885\t   28|             continue\n9886\t   29|         if not stat.S_ISREG(mode):\n9887\t   30|             raise ValueError(\"nonregular entry: \" + str(p))\n9888\t   31|         result[p.relative_to(root).as_posix()] = digest(p)\n9889\t   32|     return result\n9890\t   33| \n9891\t   34| def check(root, installed=None, destination=None):\n9892\t   35|     actual = regulars(root)\n9893\t   36|     inventory = json.loads((root / \"inventory.json\").read_text())\n9894\t   37|     expected = {r[\"path\"]: {\"sha256\": r[\"sha256\"], \"bytes\": r[\"bytes\"]} for r in inventory[\"files\"]}\n9895\t   38|     if len(expected) != len(inventory[\"files\"]):\n9896\t   39|         raise ValueError(\"duplicate inventory path\")\n9897\t   40|     actual.pop(\"inventory.json\", None)\n9898\t   41|     if actual != expected:\n9899\t   42|         raise ValueError(\"inventory mismatch: \" + json.dumps({\"missing\": sorted(set(expected)-set(actual)), \"extra\": sorted(set(actual)-set(expected)), \"changed\": sorted(k for k in set(actual)&set(expected) if actual[k]!=expected[k])}))\n9900\t   43|     skill = root / \"skills/stdo-work\"\n9901\t   44|     text = (skill / \"SKILL.md\").read_text()\n9902\t   45|     if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"):\n9903\t   46|         raise ValueError(\"missing skill frontmatter\")\n9904\t   47|     front = text.split(\"---\", 2)[1]\n9905\t   48|     if re.search(r\"(?m)^name: stdo-work$\", front) is None:\n9906\t   49|         raise ValueError(\"invalid name/folder binding\")\n9907\t   50|     if re.search(r\"(?m)^description: .+\", front) is None:\n9908\t   51|         raise ValueError(\"missing description\")\n9909\t   52|     link_count = 0\n9910\t   53|     for p in root.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n9911\t   54|         for link in re.findall(r\"\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^)]+)\\)\", p.read_text()):\n9912\t   55|             target = link.split(\"#\", 1)[0]\n9913\t   56|             if not target or \"://\" in target:\n9914\t   57|                 continue\n9915\t   58|             resolved = (p.parent / target).resolve()\n9916\t   59|             boundary = skill.resolve() if p.is_relative_to(skill) else root.resolve()\n9917\t   60|             if not resolved.is_relative_to(boundary) or not resolved.is_file():\n9918\t   61|                 raise ValueError(\"unresolvable/escaping resource: \" + str(p) + \" -> \" + link)\n9919\t   62|             link_count += 1\n9920\t   63|     routes = json.loads((skill / \"source-routes.json\").read_text())\n9921\t   64|     for source in routes[\"sources\"]:\n9922\t   65|         if not re.fullmatch(\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", source[\"sha256\"]):\n9923\t   66|             raise ValueError(\"invalid source hash\")\n9924\t   67|     if installed is not None:\n9925\t   68|         current = regulars(installed)\n9926\t   69|         subset = {p[len(\"skills/stdo-work/\"):]: v for p, v in expected.items() if p.startswith(\"skills/stdo-work/\")}\n9927\t   70|         if current != subset:\n9928\t   71|             raise ValueError(\"installed custody mismatch\")\n9929\t   72|     if destination is not None:\n9930\t   73|         safe_ancestors(destination)\n9931\t   74|         if destination.exists() or destination.resolve().is_relative_to(root.resolve()):\n9932\t   75|             raise ValueError(\"destination exists or is inside package\")\n9933\t   76|         if destination.name != \"stdo-work\" or destination.parent.name != \"skills\" or destination.parent.parent.name != \".agents\":\n9934\t   77|             raise ValueError(\"destination must be repository .agents/skills/stdo-work\")\n9935\t   78|     return {\"status\": \"passed\", \"files\": len(actual), \"local_links\": link_count, \"inventory_sha256\": digest(root/\"inventory.json\")[\"sha256\"], \"installed_checked\": installed is not None, \"destination_checked\": destination is not None, \"limits\": \"finite bytes/metadata/resources/custody only; no semantic or actual-host qualification\"}\n9936\t   79| \n9937\t   80| if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n9938\t   81|     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n9939\t   82|     parser.add_argument(\"root\", type=Path)\n9940\t   83|     parser.add_argument(\"--installed\", type=Path)\n9941\t   84|     parser.add_argument(\"--destination\", type=Path)\n9942\t   85|     args = parser.parse_args()\n9943\t   86|     try:\n9944\t   87|         print(json.dumps(check(args.root.absolute(), args.installed.absolute() if args.installed else None, args.destination.absolute() if args.destination else None), sort_keys=True))\n9945\t   88|     except (ValueError, OSError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n9946\t   89|         print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"failed\", \"error\": str(exc)}))\n9947\t   90|         raise SystemExit(1)\n9948\t   91| \n9949\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38","uuid":"988aa0fc-b90d-4bc7-965e-fceb12317277","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:12:41.286Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jim/.claude/projects/-Users-jim-src-apps-specification-methodology-skills/628dfe7c-13d9-4c76-8146-64fd9787ee38/tool-results/barha86i9.txt","content":"######## [38] product:build_tenants/codex/README.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Codex STDO work candidate\n    2| \n    3| This tenant packages one progressive skill, stdo-work. It targets the host mechanics documented for codex-cli 0.164.0 and the exact STDO v3.0.1-rc.1 basis. It is a construction candidate, not an accepted release or qualified host installation.\n    4| \n    5| Start at [SKILL.md](skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md). The [design](design/DESIGN.md) maps SK-01 through SK-12 to the algorithm, host and required proof. [Qualification](skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md) retains every Q01–Q12 obligation. Explicit invocation is `$stdo-work`; ordinary relevant tasks use host automatic discovery. Success in one lane does not establish the other.\n    6| \n    7| ## Read-only package check\n    8| \n    9| ```sh\n   10| python3 -B /absolute/path/to/codex/tests/verify_package.py /absolute/path/to/codex\n   11| ```\n   12| \n   13| The inventory binds every ordinary regular file under this tenant except inventory.json itself; retain that manifest's digest separately. Checks cover exact inventory, skill metadata, contained resolvable local resources and declared source hashes. No host/model invocation or semantic verdict follows.\n   14| \n   15| ## Repository-local installation\n   16| \n   17| Use only an authorized disposable target for initial qualification. Set the following paths to the selected exact tenant and target workspace. Keep a copy of the complete tenant and inventory outside all skill discovery roots as the install receipt.\n   18| \n   19| ```sh\n   20| set -eu\n   21| tenant=/absolute/path/to/exact/codex\n   22| target=/absolute/path/to/authorized/workspace\n   23| destination=\"$target/.agents/skills/stdo-work\"\n   24| python3 -B \"$tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$tenant\" --destination \"$destination\"\n   25| mkdir -p \"$target/.agents/skills\"\n   26| cp -R \"$tenant/skills/stdo-work\" \"$destination\"\n   27| python3 -B \"$tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$tenant\" --installed \"$destination\"\n   28| ```\n   29| \n   30| The destination preflight refuses an existing directory, symlink or symlink ancestor. It is a finite custody check, not a grant. Do not choose a target inside the package. Copy the entire skill folder; its references remain relative. Do not change global settings or install the other tenant.\n   31| \n   32| Open Codex in that workspace, observe discovery and perform a fresh explicit invocation separately. Updates are normally detected; restart if stale and keep the earlier failure. The host source is identified in the packaged source-routes.json; no automatic-discovery guarantee is made.\n   33| \n   34| ## Update or remove only the owned installation\n   35| \n   36| Retain the previous complete tenant, its inventory digest and destination as the old receipt. Before any update or removal, compare the actual installed directory against that previous package:\n   37| \n   38| ```sh\n   39| python3 -B \"$previous_tenant/tests/verify_package.py\" \"$previous_tenant\" --installed \"$destination\"\n   40| ```\n   41| \n   42| If files differ, are extra, missing, symlinked or custody is unknown, stop replacement/removal and report the conflict. Preserve local modifications and unrelated configuration.\n   43| \n   44| For update, also verify the new tenant. Move only the verified old stdo-work directory to an authorized, absent retained directory outside every discovery root, then use the installation recipe with the new tenant. Record both inventory identities. If copying is interrupted, reconcile actual files before any retry or rollback. This deliberately retains the previous selected package instead of merging directories.\n   45| \n   46| For removal after the old receipt check, remove only the exact verified destination. Do not remove its .agents/skills parent, other skills, another tenant or host configuration. Obtain a fresh directory observation after removal and retain evidence of unrelated entries. Removal and update remain unperformed Q12 host operations in this construction.\n   47| \n   48| ## Current proof limits\n   49| \n   50| The Worker records author instruction assessment and finite package checks outside this frozen package in its activation's work surface. Actual-host Q01–Q12 trials, independent review, publication and owner acceptance remain open. The original failed construction remains historical evidence; this successor neither erases it nor invents a previous successful write.\n   51| \n\n######## [39] product:build_tenants/codex/design/DESIGN.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Codex tenant design — T001 successor 1\n    2| \n    3| Recorded before implementation. Scope: build_tenants/codex and .ai-workspace/work/T001/codex/actor/successor-1 only; construction authority is successor codex/TASK.md SHA256 4c33deea408deef15ac9900f66d5986b06efefb94de40697cf249d536770845b, grant urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:2. No Product acceptance, publication or installation is claimed.\n    4| \n    5| ## Basis and source ownership\n    6| \n    7| STDO Skills common inventory a6d348b8385ea453ce29362fb9d74559304b1b91743b3c9ea31a83a9f02b5f2d governs this candidate. STDO stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8 owns the method. Its installed basis was verified by stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify on 2026-10-25. The discovery channel does not select a newer basis.\n    8| \n    9| Requirements SHA256 dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc and scenarios SHA256 089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e remain common external authority. The frame basis SHA256 00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa is selected by this activation for construction, not accepted by this Worker. Method routing comes from specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md SHA256 15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3. Installed deciding sections are acquired as needed; no copied methodology is installed.\n   10| \n   11| ## Algorithm and host binding\n   12| \n   13| One skill, stdo-work, supplies task-based discovery for an already governed workspace and explicit setup requests. Its name and description remain available to Codex; automatic invocation stays enabled by omitting any disabling policy. Only the entrypoint and the relevant reference are acquired. References are packaged inside the skill, so copying the complete directory preserves their links.\n   14| \n   15| | Requirements | Algorithm | Codex or tool mechanism | Finite proof |\n   16| |---|---|---|---|\n   17| | SK-01 | Route relevant task, ignore unrelated task, distinguish discovery from execution | SKILL.md frontmatter; repository .agents/skills/stdo-work; explicit $stdo-work | Q01, Q02, Q12 |\n   18| | SK-02 | Select one Product, verify exact installed basis, acquire bootstrap and deciding owner | stdo status --definition PATH --verify; public source.read with exact SourceRefs | Q03 |\n   19| | SK-03 | Reuse sufficient authority; choose direct Writer for a sufficient small effect; coordinate only on material boundary | Codex reasoning over acquired contract; host actors only where selected and admitted | Q04, Q05 |\n   20| | SK-04 | Discover exact schemas, call required operation, retain actual response and effect evidence | ordinary public a_c CLI, complete JSON envelope on stdin; MCP optional | Q01, Q06, Q08 |\n   21| | SK-05 | Preserve smallest deciding causal context including retained obligations and differing histories | exact SourceRefs, context.assemble when selected; activation carrier | Q05, Q07 |\n   22| | SK-06 | Bind child outcome, basis, territory, proof, consumer and stop; consume closed return before next activation | configured contract.preflight, dispatch.start/observe and return.capture/check where admitted; no invented tool | Q04, Q05 |\n   23| | SK-07 | Derive expected behavior from source before exact candidate; retain exposure and family limits | review.prepare where selected; fresh separately admitted reviewer; source.read | Q05, Q09 |\n   24| | SK-08 | Reacquire current evidence, reconcile uncertain effects before retry, retain unaffected evidence | workspace.observe, source.read, evidence.read, granted recovery path | Q07-Q10 |\n   25| | SK-09 | Separate candidate availability, assessment, consumer disposition, acceptance | declared closed return schema, original basis, explicit residuals and not_performed | Q06, Q09, Q10 |\n   26| | SK-10 | Prepare exact immutable candidate; act only on authorized release destination; scoped package install/update/remove | selected release tool discovered from its contract; file-copy deployment only with corresponding grant | Q11, Q12 |\n   27| | SK-11 | Package references together; inventory exact content; retain previous identity on update | read-only package verifier; owned-directory installation recipe | Q12 |\n   28| | SK-12 | Freeze substantive tasks and independent oracle, preserve every attempt and unknown costs | qualification plan and actual host traces, not keyword success grading | Q01-Q12 |\n   29| \n   30| Codex mechanics are independently sourced in operator codex/HOST.md SHA256 6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e: codex-cli 0.164.0, repository-local .agents/skills discovery, explicit $skill-name, relative references, restart when discovery is stale. Configured model/effort gpt-6-astra/max is inherited; actual resolution is unknown unless the run records it. No nested actor is launched in this construction.\n   31| \n   32| ## Tool boundary and failure behavior\n   33| \n   34| Native method profile urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1 SHA256 a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7 is selected. tools.describe reports provisional construction support, not qualification. Its builder identity v2.5.1-rc.2 is distinct from this selected operation binding. There is no supported native results.conjoin. Executive consumption is F_P under its granted relation; any decision must preserve required predicates, applicability, incompatible bases and unresolved contradictions.\n   35| \n   36| Host reads, SHA256 computation and static package checks are declared auxiliary mechanics. They establish byte/structure facts only and never replace required source.read, workspace.observe, work.write, admission or assessment results. All current construction deliverables are written with work.write, own observation and exact preimage; postimage and OperationEvidence are then read. Unknown completion stops dependent writing pending reconciliation.\n   37| \n   38| A failed required operation withholds its dependent claim. Independent work can continue under its existing grant. No automatic retries, authorization renewal or publication follow from successful transport. A missing installation or ambiguous Product is a basis problem, not a request to adopt latest. An unperformed assessment has no core result; performed inconclusive assessment is indeterminate; construction without an output is incomplete for candidate availability.\n   39| \n   40| ## Installation and qualification\n   41| \n   42| README supplies a repository-local, single-directory copy recipe and explicit update/removal custody checks. No installer mutates host configuration implicitly. A read-only verifier checks packaged resources and optional observed inventory. It does not assess instruction semantics or host discovery.\n   43| \n   44| Q01-Q12 actual host trials, source-first independent assessment, release and owner acceptance remain unperformed here. The qualification plan keeps each case/lane visible and preserves failures. Static checks support only packaging integrity; they do not justify automatic-selection reliability or efficiency claims.\n   45| \n   46| ## Successor construction decisions\n   47| \n   48| The earlier text was a refused proposal, not an adopted design. HISTORY.json retains that failure and does not prove universal external-effect absence. This new activation authorizes scoped ordinary mkdir and the repaired public CLI. This design is written before implementation under that new grant. The current Worker reran the manager verification successfully and acquired all common deciding sources through public source.read.\n   49| \n   50| Deliver one stdo-work/SKILL.md with references/basis.md, tools.md, delegation.md, recovery.md, release-install.md and qualification.md. A package-local source-routes.json preserves exact source locators without copying the method. The tenant README carries installation commands; tests/verify_package.py performs only read-only finite metadata, contained-path, resource and inventory checks. inventory.json freezes all tenant regular files except itself; its own digest is returned separately. Assessment/transition records stay in the actor territory so the assessed package remains frozen. Every artifact content uses work.write after current containing-directory observation; allowed host mkdir checks every ancestor for symlinks. No peer or global effects, nested model calls or installation happen in this construction.\n   51| \n   52| The skill uses the host mechanics acquired from HOST.md and local skill-authoring guidance. These establish documented instruction paths only. The declared 0.164.0 host remains the qualification target; automatic discovery, explicit invocation, model resolution and installation behavior require actual later trials. Existing tool responses establish supported schemas and narrow operation output, not automatic semantic acceptance. The public tools.describe response and all writes retain OperationEvidence. Required operation failure stops its dependent branch with the actual cause.\n   53| \n\n######## [40] product:build_tenants/codex/inventory.json sel=None ########\n    1| {\n    2|   \"schema\": \"stdo-skills.codex.candidate-inventory/1\",\n    3|   \"activation\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:2\",\n    4|   \"scope\": \"all ordinary regular files under build_tenants/codex except this inventory; inventory digest returned separately\",\n    5|   \"files\": [\n    6|     {\n    7|       \"path\": \"README.md\",\n    8|       \"sha256\": \"0ee72656c36d7fb0dc5d6cc10ea9b7b4bfa04e8152dbb54ff8434714e83029c1\",\n    9|       \"bytes\": 4048\n   10|     },\n   11|     {\n   12|       \"path\": \"design/DESIGN.md\",\n   13|       \"sha256\": \"b051cc738cc6e9a7d80a3c13e0ad6887fe64f01a8d1f87cce4a0ceb5aa7caca9\",\n   14|       \"bytes\": 8835\n   15|     },\n   16|     {\n   17|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md\",\n   18|       \"sha256\": \"ba6f7ab1e6de875e2f019b049f7817e771474f1b511a74fe2392a55a37078ee8\",\n   19|       \"bytes\": 3116\n   20|     },\n   21|     {\n   22|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md\",\n   23|       \"sha256\": \"7b409d4895e7be3291e4e41c32e497ae045e9fb4b62f01b9622b10888d449cda\",\n   24|       \"bytes\": 2694\n   25|     },\n   26|     {\n   27|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md\",\n   28|       \"sha256\": \"0bb621b4d6edb17f2100878a567596f85a52b517edfafbb2ceba7119dce8bfde\",\n   29|       \"bytes\": 2969\n   30|     },\n   31|     {\n   32|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md\",\n   33|       \"sha256\": \"dda296ed053f3e8ed5ab4cdc7c7b9f162754832fc89ded9280044d96f9dc795c\",\n   34|       \"bytes\": 3001\n   35|     },\n   36|     {\n   37|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md\",\n   38|       \"sha256\": \"d7f7f118eea492bb64456a56c4cb4987e6e23acd8b3c0143ba87cf5ec9a92c80\",\n   39|       \"bytes\": 3010\n   40|     },\n   41|     {\n   42|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md\",\n   43|       \"sha256\": \"ec7cb5a407f6690936d0bf79ab5fc8796c2cfca4c34772f61ceff4b68f337cfb\",\n   44|       \"bytes\": 2422\n   45|     },\n   46|     {\n   47|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md\",\n   48|       \"sha256\": \"8bb49c0dfe0eb87fbfbe5063c4a43e15f074e25fdd4ff90ffdec24ef14e75c8b\",\n   49|       \"bytes\": 4116\n   50|     },\n   51|     {\n   52|       \"path\": \"skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json\",\n   53|       \"sha256\": \"09972e4af512645c43207aa3edd5114e1e81c24ef344c76a6af2e99852920403\",\n   54|       \"bytes\": 3501\n   55|     },\n   56|     {\n   57|       \"path\": \"tests/verify_package.py\",\n   58|       \"sha256\": \"65ec9851967a60ab6f25f4c988b2ddbc05642ce44ae71401d6f1bf99f5ec0086\",\n   59|       \"bytes\": 4512\n   60|     }\n   61|   ]\n   62| }\n   63| \n\n######## [41] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md sel=None ########\n    1| ---\n    2| name: stdo-work\n    3| description: Apply a selected STDO method to governed software work, including setup, scoped changes, independent review, recovery and release preparation. Use for tasks in an STDO workspace or explicit STDO setup; do not impose STDO on unrelated requests.\n    4| ---\n    5| \n    6| # STDO work\n    7| \n    8| Help the user complete the requested work under the selected Product and exact method. This package targets STDO v3.0.1-rc.1; its manifest and source routes are in [basis](references/basis.md). It supplies instructions, not authority.\n    9| \n   10| 1. Identify the outcome and changed owner: requirement, design, implementation, assessment or release. Select exactly one applicable Product Definition, or an explicitly authorized cross-Product relation. Read the applicable local bootstrap and deciding sources. If an activated Context already supplies the exact binding, use it and acquire only its missing material sources.\n   11| 2. Verify the pinned installation and operation compatibility through [basis](references/basis.md) and [tools](references/tools.md). Preserve sufficient existing authorization. Ask only for a material missing decision, not repeated consent for already granted work.\n   12| 3. Choose the smallest sufficient path. For an authorized one-file correction with adequate requirement/design, enter the bound direct Writer path: acquire current preimage, make only that effect through its declared tool, perform focused proof and return to its consumer. Do not require a new ticket, Executive or independent reviewer solely because work exists.\n   13| 4. Use [delegation](references/delegation.md) when a material context, capability, ownership or required independence boundary calls for it. An Executive coordinates without mutating; a separately granted Worker/Writer implements. Do not launch actors unless the current grant permits them.\n   14| 5. Make the requested change and inspect actual responses and postimages. Read [recovery](references/recovery.md) on continuation, interruption, refusal or stale evidence. An unsupported required tool withholds the dependent claim. An uncertain effect must be reconciled before repeating it.\n   15| 6. Return the exact candidate, source/basis identities, actual proof, failures, remaining obligations and invalidators. Keep availability, author assessment, independent review and owner acceptance separate. For release/install work use [release and installation](references/release-install.md); for behavior qualification use [qualification](references/qualification.md).\n   16| \n   17| Normal invocation: ask for the relevant task in a governed workspace. Explicit invocation: `$stdo-work Correct the named file under the existing grant`. The host may discover the description automatically; acquisition and success must be observed separately. If explicit invocation works after failed automatic discovery, retain both attempts.\n   18| \n   19| Read only the reference needed for the current branch. Common requirements and method owners remain external authority; [source routes](source-routes.json) identify this package's construction basis. A target workspace supplies its own Product Definition, sources and grants.\n   20| \n\n######## [42] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Bind the exact workspace and method\n    2| \n    3| Run the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n    4| \n    5| ```sh\n    6| stdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n    7| ```\n    8| \n    9| Inspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n   10| \n   11| Resolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n   12| \n   13| | Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n   14| |---|---|\n   15| | Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n   16| | WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n   17| | Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n   18| | Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n   19| | Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n   20| | Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n   21| | Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n   22| | Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n   23| | Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n   24| | Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n   25| | Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n   26| \n   27| These are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n   28| \n   29| Record the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n   30| \n\n######## [43] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/delegation.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Bounded handoff and independent review\n    2| \n    3| Use delegation only when required by a material boundary and authorized by the current configuration. A sufficient direct Writer task goes straight from current basis/grant to the exact effect and focused proof; no automatic coordination or review gate is added.\n    4| \n    5| Before handoff retain:\n    6| - Exact outcome and subject; Product Definition and immutable method; governing requirement and design; changed producer, transport, consumer and artifact relations.\n    7| - Frame id/revision and result algebra; activation identity; operation grant and precise territory; separate semantic, evaluation, decision, acceptance and publication authorities.\n    8| - Required evidence and predicates; admissible source routes; retained failures/counterexamples; original observations and their provenance.\n    9| - Host/tool implementation and method support; actor/context/resource limits and exclusions; stop/change invalidators; return schema and named consumer.\n   10| \n   11| Select only the smallest dependency-ready reference frontier that preserves those distinctions. If it does not fit the envelope, refine or sequence within existing authority; seek the actual missing capability or envelope decision when needed. Do not erase material obligations to fit.\n   12| \n   13| Discover the supported `context.assemble`, `contract.preflight`, `dispatch.start`, `dispatch.observe`, `return.capture` and `return.check` contracts through the public path in [tools](tools.md), selecting only operations required by this activation. A missing supported binding stops the dependent handoff. Do not replace the selected dispatch with a native spawn just because it exists. Retain the actual input delivery, process result, stdout/stderr and parsed original closed return. Transport success and actor output availability do not establish requested effects or fitness.\n   14| \n   15| Workers implement only their grant, self-assess the exact candidate and return. They do not activate the next stage. Executive consumes closed results and selects only an already authorized next action; if a record must be written, bind a Writer rather than mutating in the Executive frame.\n   16| \n   17| A required Reviewer acquires governing sources and derives expected behavior before the exact candidate and proof. Use a fresh permitted reviewer and retain actual exposure, author relationship, model family/resolution and limitations. Nonauthor same-family review does not prove cross-family independence. Where a review.prepare tool is selected, actually call its supported contract. The Reviewer reports findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty; it does not implement the adopted repair or decide promotion. After material repair, withdraw only affected old reliance and obtain the required fresh assessment.\n   18| \n   19| A returned candidate_ready concerns availability. Assessments keep their own predicates and results. Owner disposition is a separate act. Contradictory results require disposition, not majority voting.\n   20| \n\n######## [44] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/qualification.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Qualification boundary\n    2| \n    3| Common requirements and scenarios remain exact external authority in [source routes](../source-routes.json). Derive expected outcomes independently before acquiring the tenant answer. Freeze an isolated workspace, exact source/package/tool/method cuts, authority, host/model/settings, input exposure, time/resource bound and lane. Automatic discovery and explicit invocation are separate attempts; a fallback never erases an automatic failure.\n    4| \n    5| | Required case | Evidence needed; current construction standing |\n    6| |---|---|\n    7| | Q01 | Ordinary request discovers skill and performs bounded tool-backed change; fresh explicit lane; actual host unperformed |\n    8| | Q02 | Unrelated task avoids forced STDO setup; actual host unperformed |\n    9| | Q03 | Valid pin and missing/altered/ambiguous variants; actual host variants unperformed |\n   10| | Q04 | Sufficient one-file direct Writer uses focused proof without invented ticket/coordination/review; author walkthrough only |\n   11| | Q05 | Actual worker handoff and source-first independent reviewer; unperformed |\n   12| | Q06 | Actual unsupported/error response retained and dependent success withheld; host trials unperformed |\n   13| | Q07 | Equal bytes with accepted history versus unresolved counterexample cause distinct continuation; author walkthrough only |\n   14| | Q08 | Changed target with lost acknowledgment reconciled before retry; host trial unperformed |\n   15| | Q09 | Material source/candidate change withdraws affected review reliance only; unperformed |\n   16| | Q10 | Incomplete availability, inconclusive assessment and unperformed assessment remain distinct; unperformed |\n   17| | Q11 | Preparation-only authority and separately authorized local deployment; unperformed |\n   18| | Q12 | Scoped install/invoke/update/remove with resource and unrelated-config checks; unperformed |\n   19| \n   20| Retain each actual invocation, input delivery, source acquisition, output, tool trace, effect/postimage, per-predicate verdict and counterexample, residual and invalidator. Measure elapsed time and reported tokens/cost; unavailable data stays unknown. Include retries, repair and review in total cost and compare equivalent substantive information. One successful trial is bounded evidence, not a reliability estimate or general efficiency benefit.\n   21| \n   22| Run the cheapest focused check capable of falsifying the current change; expensive whole-candidate host qualification belongs at its declared boundary. The read-only package verifier checks actual metadata, resource containment and file inventory. It does not grade semantic success by keywords. Author instruction assessment must separately inspect the actual bodies and reason through Q04, Q07 and Q06/Q08. Independent review and all mandatory host cases remain necessary for initial delivery; construction cannot silently waive them.\n   23| \n   24| Host/tool/method or prompt changes identify affected trials and claims. Retain unaffected evidence with a justified currentness relation. Tune from observed failures rather than accumulating universal process.\n   25| \n\n######## [45] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/recovery.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Resume from evidence\n    2| \n    3| On restart acquire the current target, material governing sources, grant, operation records and retained return/effect evidence. Preserve their original identities and distinguish historical acquisition from fresh observation. Compare the changed inputs and apply only affected invalidators.\n    4| \n    5| For identical candidate bytes with different histories, do not produce the same continuation automatically:\n    6| - A current applicable accepted assessment may support the next already authorized action.\n    7| - An unresolved counterexample that defeats that assessment withholds the dependent claim. Preserve the obligation, reacquire its deciding source, and route to the required repair or reassessment owner. Equal file hashes cannot erase it.\n    8| \n    9| After a timeout or lost acknowledgment:\n   10| 1. Retain the original request/attempt id and unknown-effect state. Do not resend it or infer rollback.\n   11| 2. Acquire a new workspace.observe of the target and read the original operation/effect evidence with evidence.read.\n   12| 3. If intended postimage and qualified completion evidence agree, consume that single effect without repeating it.\n   13| 4. If only changed bytes are visible, establish their custody and intended-effect relation; unrelated matching bytes alone do not close it. If absence is established, retry only through the declared recovery contract and existing authority. Otherwise return the unreconciled effect and missing observation. Process end alone does not prove descendant/external end.\n   14| \n   15| For unsupported method, execution error or missing acquisition retain the actual refusal/error. Withhold dependent success, name the precise re-entry (tool owner, basis owner or operation owner), and preserve useful partial artifacts. Continue only independent authorized work. Do not silently switch tools or repeat an uncertain effect.\n   16| \n   17| Use the selected return contract. Under this native binding:\n   18| - candidate_ready: exact candidate plus transition evidence exists; not a fitness result.\n   19| - incomplete: activated construction ended without its needed output; its availability is falsified, with stop cause and residuals.\n   20| - refused: an applicable prohibition or owner-valid refusal defeats construction.\n   21| - re_entry_requested: name basis or authority cause; map materially unusable basis to invalid_basis and missing authority to out_of_frame.\n   22| - A performed assessment returns satisfied, falsified with counterexample, indeterminate on undecidable admissible evidence, invalid_basis, or out_of_frame as warranted.\n   23| - An unperformed assessment has no result and belongs in not_performed.\n   24| \n   25| Close with original frame, activation, subject, method/observation basis, actor and consumer. Add exact current artifact/effect evidence without replacing the original activation basis. Retain failed attempts and unknown costs. After source/tool/host/grant/candidate changes or a counterexample, invalidate only affected reliance with its cause and preserve unrelated valid evidence. Never declare acceptance from test totals.\n   26| \n\n######## [46] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/release-install.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Release preparation and scoped deployment\n    2| \n    3| Acquire RELEASE.md and IDENTITY.md from the verified installation and the target Product's release conditions. Bind exact candidate inventory, evidence, acceptance/disposition requirements, destination and publication grant. With a preparation-only grant, assemble a reviewable local artifact and return it; no remote publication follows. Do not invent a second final cut to fix an identity problem. Discover and actually use the release tool contract selected by that Product; unsupported release tooling leaves publication unperformed.\n    4| \n    5| This skill's deployment unit is the entire stdo-work directory. Its repository-local destination is exactly TARGET/.agents/skills/stdo-work. It neither installs the Claude tenant nor modifies host defaults. The tenant README documents the executable package verifier and copy recipe. At deployment time:\n    6| 1. Freeze the package inventory, verify all ordinary regular files and internal resources, and retain the chosen identity outside the discovery directory.\n    7| 2. Verify the target grant and every destination ancestor: no symlink, escape or unexpected existing stdo-work. Resolve duplicate skill names deliberately; names are not merged.\n    8| 3. Install only that directory. Record destination, exact file inventory and old/new package identities in the authorized work surface.\n    9| 4. Open Codex in that workspace. Exercise ordinary discovery and explicit $stdo-work invocation as separate trials. Confirm acquisition and required tool events. If stale, restart and retain the failed discovery attempt.\n   10| 5. For update, compare the entire installed file set and hashes to the retained old receipt before replacement. If locally changed or ownership unknown, stop that replacement and report the conflict; do not overwrite it. Retain the old package outside all discovery roots and its identity for deliberate rollback.\n   11| 6. Remove only the owned selected stdo-work directory after the same receipt check. Preserve .agents/skills, other skills and configuration. Unknown files or hashes block destructive removal. Recheck the remaining unrelated configuration.\n   12| \n   13| These instructions specify a deployable path. Finite package checks do not prove discovery, actual installation, update or removal behavior; Q12 remains open until performed in an authorized disposable host workspace. Installation does not constitute method adoption or Product acceptance.\n   14| \n\n######## [47] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md sel=None ########\n    1| # Public tool path\n    2| \n    3| Use the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n    4| \n    5| The ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n    6| \n    7| This executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n    8| \n    9| ```sh\n   10| \"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n   11|   --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n   12|   call --request - <<'JSON'\n   13| {\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\n   14| JSON\n   15| ```\n   16| \n   17| Set AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n   18| \n   19| Acquisition envelope arguments:\n   20| ```json\n   21| {\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n   22| ```\n   23| Use operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n   24| \n   25| For an authorized write:\n   26| 1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n   27| 2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n   28| 3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n   29| 4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n   30| \n   31| For `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n   32| \n   33| For context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n   34| \n   35| Auxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n   36| \n\n######## [48] product:build_tenants/codex/skills/stdo-work/source-routes.json sel=None ########\n    1| {\n    2|   \"schema\": \"stdo-skills.codex.source-routes/1\",\n    3|   \"standing\": \"construction provenance; target workspace supplies its own definition and grants\",\n    4|   \"method\": {\n    5|     \"uri\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\",\n    6|     \"manifest_sha256\": \"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\"\n    7|   },\n    8|   \"sources\": [\n    9|     {\n   10|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   11|       \"object\": null,\n   12|       \"path\": \"specification/PRODUCT.md\",\n   13|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   14|       \"selector\": null,\n   15|       \"sha256\": \"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\"\n   16|     },\n   17|     {\n   18|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   19|       \"object\": null,\n   20|       \"path\": \"specification/INTENT.md\",\n   21|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   22|       \"selector\": null,\n   23|       \"sha256\": \"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\"\n   24|     },\n   25|     {\n   26|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   27|       \"object\": null,\n   28|       \"path\": \"specification/requirements/README.md\",\n   29|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   30|       \"selector\": null,\n   31|       \"sha256\": \"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\"\n   32|     },\n   33|     {\n   34|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   35|       \"object\": null,\n   36|       \"path\": \"specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md\",\n   37|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   38|       \"selector\": null,\n   39|       \"sha256\": \"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\"\n   40|     },\n   41|     {\n   42|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   43|       \"object\": null,\n   44|       \"path\": \"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\n   45|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   46|       \"selector\": null,\n   47|       \"sha256\": \"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\"\n   48|     },\n   49|     {\n   50|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   51|       \"object\": null,\n   52|       \"path\": \"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\",\n   53|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   54|       \"selector\": null,\n   55|       \"sha256\": \"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\"\n   56|     },\n   57|     {\n   58|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   59|       \"object\": null,\n   60|       \"path\": \"stdo_skills.json\",\n   61|       \"root\": \"product\",\n   62|       \"selector\": null,\n   63|       \"sha256\": \"4339a7dbc735052c08962154966fc13a4e30206d42ba2e80b53c6009a5008c22\"\n   64|     },\n   65|     {\n   66|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   67|       \"object\": null,\n   68|       \"path\": \"codex/HOST.md\",\n   69|       \"root\": \"successor\",\n   70|       \"selector\": null,\n   71|       \"sha256\": \"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\"\n   72|     },\n   73|     {\n   74|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   75|       \"object\": null,\n   76|       \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n   77|       \"root\": \"method\",\n   78|       \"selector\": {\n   79|         \"lines\": [\n   80|           1750,\n   81|           1768\n   82|         ]\n   83|       },\n   84|       \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n   85|     },\n   86|     {\n   87|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n   88|       \"object\": null,\n   89|       \"path\": \"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\n   90|       \"root\": \"method\",\n   91|       \"selector\": {\n   92|         \"lines\": [\n   93|           1004,\n   94|           1055\n   95|         ]\n   96|       },\n   97|       \"sha256\": \"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"\n   98|     },\n   99|     {\n  100|       \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n  101|       \"object\": null,\n  102|       \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\",\n  103|       \"root\": \"tool\",\n  104|       \"selector\": null,\n  105|       \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"\n  106|     }\n  107|   ],\n  108|   \"resolution\": \"Root aliases require the active exact policy. Resolve method under the verified installation, common construction sources under the STDO Skills source project. Missing provenance routes do not authorize substitution.\"\n  109| }\n  110| \n\n######## [49] product:build_tenants/codex/tests/verify_package.py sel=None ########\n    1| \"\"\"Read-only finite package, resource and installation-custody checks.\"\"\"\n    2| import argparse\n    3| import hashlib\n    4| import json\n    5| import re\n    6| import stat\n    7| from pathlib import Path\n    8| \n    9| def digest(path):\n   10|     data = path.read_bytes()\n   11|     return {\"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), \"bytes\": len(data)}\n   12| \n   13| def safe_ancestors(path):\n   14|     for p in [path, *path.parents]:\n   15|         if p.is_symlink():\n   16|             raise ValueError(\"symlink refused: \" + str(p))\n   17| \n   18| def regulars(root):\n   19|     safe_ancestors(root)\n   20|     if not root.is_dir():\n   21|         raise ValueError(\"missing directory: \" + str(root))\n   22|     result = {}\n   23|     for p in sorted(root.rglob(\"*\")):\n   24|         mode = p.lstat().st_mode\n   25|         if stat.S_ISLNK(mode):\n   26|             raise ValueError(\"symlink refused: \" + str(p))\n   27|         if stat.S_ISDIR(mode):\n   28|             continue\n   29|         if not stat.S_ISREG(mode):\n   30|             raise ValueError(\"nonregular entry: \" + str(p))\n   31|         result[p.relative_to(root).as_posix()] = digest(p)\n   32|     return result\n   33| \n   34| def check(root, installed=None, destination=None):\n   35|     actual = regulars(root)\n   36|     inventory = json.loads((root / \"inventory.json\").read_text())\n   37|     expected = {r[\"path\"]: {\"sha256\": r[\"sha256\"], \"bytes\": r[\"bytes\"]} for r in inventory[\"files\"]}\n   38|     if len(expected) != len(inventory[\"files\"]):\n   39|         raise ValueError(\"duplicate inventory path\")\n   40|     actual.pop(\"inventory.json\", None)\n   41|     if actual != expected:\n   42|         raise ValueError(\"inventory mismatch: \" + json.dumps({\"missing\": sorted(set(expected)-set(actual)), \"extra\": sorted(set(actual)-set(expected)), \"changed\": sorted(k for k in set(actual)&set(expected) if actual[k]!=expected[k])}))\n   43|     skill = root / \"skills/stdo-work\"\n   44|     text = (skill / \"SKILL.md\").read_text()\n   45|     if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"):\n   46|         raise ValueError(\"missing skill frontmatter\")\n   47|     front = text.split(\"---\", 2)[1]\n   48|     if re.search(r\"(?m)^name: stdo-work$\", front) is None:\n   49|         raise ValueError(\"invalid name/folder binding\")\n   50|     if re.search(r\"(?m)^description: .+\", front) is None:\n   51|         raise ValueError(\"missing description\")\n   52|     link_count = 0\n   53|     for p in root.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n   54|         for link in re.findall(r\"\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^)]+)\\)\", p.read_text()):\n   55|             target = link.split(\"#\", 1)[0]\n   56|             if not target or \"://\" in target:\n   57|                 continue\n   58|             resolved = (p.parent / target).resolve()\n   59|             boundary = skill.resolve() if p.is_relative_to(skill) else root.resolve()\n   60|             if not resolved.is_relative_to(boundary) or not resolved.is_file():\n   61|                 raise ValueError(\"unresolvable/escaping resource: \" + str(p) + \" -> \" + link)\n   62|             link_count += 1\n   63|     routes = json.loads((skill / \"source-routes.json\").read_text())\n   64|     for source in routes[\"sources\"]:\n   65|         if not re.fullmatch(\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", source[\"sha256\"]):\n   66|             raise ValueError(\"invalid source hash\")\n   67|     if installed is not None:\n   68|         current = regulars(installed)\n   69|         subset = {p[len(\"skills/stdo-work/\"):]: v for p, v in expected.items() if p.startswith(\"skills/stdo-work/\")}\n   70|         if current != subset:\n   71|             raise ValueError(\"installed custody mismatch\")\n   72|     if destination is not None:\n   73|         safe_ancestors(destination)\n   74|         if destination.exists() or destination.resolve().is_relative_to(root.resolve()):\n   75|             raise ValueError(\"destination exists or is inside package\")\n   76|         if destination.name != \"stdo-work\" or destination.parent.name != \"skills\" or destination.parent.parent.name != \".agents\":\n   77|             raise ValueError(\"destination must be repository .agents/skills/stdo-work\")\n   78|     return {\"status\": \"passed\", \"files\": len(actual), \"local_links\": link_count, \"inventory_sha256\": digest(root/\"inventory.json\")[\"sha256\"], \"installed_checked\": installed is not None, \"destination_checked\": destination is not None, \"limits\": \"finite bytes/metadata/resources/custody only; no semantic or actual-host qualification\"}\n   79| \n   80| if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   81|     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   82|     parser.add_argument(\"root\", type=Path)\n   83|     parser.add_argument(\"--installed\", type=Path)\n   84|     parser.add_argument(\"--destination\", type=Path)\n   85|     args = parser.parse_args()\n   86|     try:\n   87|         print(json.dumps(check(args.root.absolute(), args.installed.absolute() if args.installed else None, args.destination.absolute() if args.destination else None), sort_keys=True))\n   88|     except (ValueError, OSError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n   89|         print(json.dumps({\"status\": \"failed\", \"error\": str(exc)}))\n   90|         raise SystemExit(1)\n   91| \n","numLines":563,"startLine":9387,"totalLines":9949}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T5tkWat6wPJcfXnsfvfUmh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
