tive-tool-codex:frozen-review:1\",\"sha256\":\"d8f28b11b8ed7b109e8f1f27d487ab74802f942551d77cd4668eb7529f3e2af0\"},\"basis\":{\"method_profile\":{\"id\":\"urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1\",\"sha256\":\"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"},\"observations\":[{\"id\":\"sha256:048c44c5602ecfc8c76a7c16c0bf86636bcccfe54da7fe9ec74f2ec4e7e82c01\",\"sha256\":\"048c44c5602ecfc8c76a7c16c0bf86636bcccfe54da7fe9ec74f2ec4e7e82c01\"}]},\"actor\":{\"id\":\"urn:stdo-skills:T001:claude:reviewer:1\",\"family\":\"anthropic-claude\",\"authorship\":\"Nonauthor cross-family Reviewer; continuous declared identity across source and candidate phases\"},\"consumer\":\"root-executive\",\"evaluations\":[{\"id\":\"candidate-assessment\",\"predicate\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"PREDICATES.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"84c3436e6e3797f973ec7e98684fecfe6936bdcd4037c581a877edbaac5fa901\"},\"domain_outcome\":{\"continuity\":\"Same Reviewer identity as the source-only phases. Expectation artifact sha256:9ed61889acb0caaec032092f45fbfa888ea63b6ae74b0be56d1301990c67bc4a was re-acquired through evidence.read (OperationEvidence sha256:6e10b4216d241c47c400c7a7186355018c2f4c1d8b64f8c1265e91882a7a2447) before any candidate byte: producer urn:stdo-skills:T001:claude:reviewer:1, nine source_inputs unchanged, source_first_observed true, prior []. The candidate was acquired exactly once by review.prepare phase=candidate (request claude-review-candidate-acquire-1, OperationEvidence sha256:ec9d5d5cc3709f9ddd6d3d9aff61dd8e5e70af48efbc8f62dafb6fb75613a2f1): population_complete true, 36 candidate files plus 9 governing, 4 proof and CLAIM, exposure [], gaps [], expectations bound and returned unchanged as result.artifact. The expectation text was used unchanged; no post-exposure intervention.\",\"exposure_disclosure\":\"Retained from the expectation phase: host bootstrap (apps-root and repository-root CLAUDE.md, git status naming modified a_c paths and untracked stdo_skills/, memory index), CLAIM/SELECTION coordinates and author metadata, and tools.describe runtime output. New in this phase: the a_c CLI used to perform this review is the native301 candidate itself; its observed runtime behaviour across both phases is admitted as actual-path evidence for component B and also makes the instrument part of the subject. external_exposure remains unknown to the tools; semantic independence is not certified by role name, family label or this return.\",\"authorship\":\"Frozen custody (SELECTION.authors, CODEX-CUSTODY.json) gives openai-codex authorship for all three components: /root/skills_common_writer, /root/skills_tool_binding_assessment, urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:worker:2; exact resolved backend unreported for the first two. No adopted Claude-authored text was found in the 36 inspected files. CODEX-CUSTODY.json sits under a Claude operator path but is mechanical custody evidence (digests, process check), reused with provenance, not as judgment. ASSESSMENT.json is constructor self-assessment and was not used as oracle.\",\"components\":[{\"id\":\"common-what\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"bound\":\"No actionable S0-S2 defect on the 12 inspected common files against expectations A1-A6 and the acquired 3.0.1 clauses; this is not acceptance, qualification or a claim about unread owners.\",\"evidence\":\"A1: one exact identity everywhere: stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364… at PRODUCT.md:23-27, AGENTS.md:5-7, CLAUDE.md:5-7, README.md:13-16, SOURCE_OWNERS.md:3-5, REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md:10-11; explicit no-latest adoption at AGENTS.md:8, PRODUCT.md:29, requirements/README.md:21-23. A2: SOURCE_OWNERS.md:6-7 routes without duplicating; REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md:38-40 adopts ACTIVATION result refinements rather than a local algebra; the S0-S4 scale at REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md:82-86 is the Product-selected scale EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §10 expects; the same-family independence declaration at REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md:93-97 is the declaration EVALUATION §3 (lines 236-240 of the acquired text) requires the governing basis to state. A3: SK-01..12 at requirements/README.md:8-117 name no host mechanism; build_tenants/README.md:3-6 is the registry; PRODUCT.md:48-51 and build_tenants/README.md:19-22 keep host mechanics in tenant HOW. A4: PRODUCT.md:81-84, GOALS.md:26-27, INTENT.md:13-15. A5: candidate status at PRODUCT.md:3, AGENTS.md:15-17, T-001:3,55-58; owner acceptance at PRODUCT.md:88-94,102-112. A6: owner outcome recorded at T-001:8-19 and INTENT.md:8-11; SCENARIOS.md:9-23 forbids counting and keyword grading.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"README.md:13, GOALS.md:6 (\\\"STDO 3.0.1 RC1\\\") versus INTENT.md:9 (\\\"released STDO 3.0.1\\\"), build_tenants/README.md:9 (\\\"pinned STDO 3.0.1 basis\\\")\",\"relation\":\"USER-OUTCOME.md:321 owner instruction \\\"pin stdo 3.0.1 as the static released methodology\\\" and A1 exact-identity expectation\",\"evidence\":\"The pinned cut is the release-candidate v3.0.1-rc.1; the exact URI and manifest are stated where identity matters, but prose labels alternate between 3.0.1 and 3.0.1 RC1.\",\"consequence\":\"No identity ambiguity for tools (manifest-bound), but whether an RC cut satisfies the owner's \\\"3.0.1\\\" is an owner question not recorded as decided in the inspected surfaces. Evidence only; no repair authored.\",\"cause\":\"inference: owner wording predates the RC selection\"},{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"README.md:27-31, REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md:53 (E03 \\\"unresolved\\\"), T-001:83\",\"relation\":\"Live surfaces present tense; currentness across the frozen claim population\",\"evidence\":\"The same frozen claim contains the native 3.0.1 tool increment (fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json status bounded-native-binding-candidate), yet no common surface references that candidate; README.md:27 still describes only the RC9 binding.\",\"consequence\":\"A reader of the common WHAT alone does not learn a native binding candidate exists. Truthful as to non-acceptance; stale as to existence. Limited consequence.\"},{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"requirements/README.md:8-117\",\"relation\":\"A6 traceability expectation\",\"evidence\":\"SK-01..12 carry no per-requirement owner-clause reference; routing is by concern in SOURCE_OWNERS.md:9-23.\",\"consequence\":\"Owner trace is recoverable by concern, not by requirement id; no acquired 3.0.1 clause mandates per-requirement citation, so this is an observation, not a violation.\"}]},{\"id\":\"native301-auth-increment\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"bound\":\"No actionable S0-S2 defect on the selected method-binding and credential-routing paths; traced by targeted inspection of ac_support.py, grep-located paths in ac_support_core.py and ac_support_effects.py, actor_cli.py, prepare_readonly.py, both design files, the binding requirement and three test files, plus actual CLI behaviour across this review. Not a whole-a_c or F_D qualification; full line read of the two large modules was not performed.\",\"evidence\":\"B1: ac_support_core.py:37 NATIVE_PROFILE_ID; core from_policy at ac_support_core.py:445-547 refuses basis_stale unless the consumer definition /constitution/stdo/basis is the exact 3.0.1 URI and manifest (core:544-547), confirmed by test_ac_support_native301.py:52-60; fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json:15-18 keeps builder v2.5.1-rc.2 separate; member digests at fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json:31,50,58,65,72 equal the acquired governing SourceRef digests for ACTIVATION, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE, AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS, EVALUATION and SPEC_METHOD, and FOUNDATIONS 92fe2f3c… appears as source_parent in every observed response; legacy packet refused basis_stale (test_ac_support_native301.py:46-50). B2: fixed allowlist ac_support_core.py:336 _ENVIRONMENT_PASSTHROUGH = {CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN}; validation ac_support_core.py:339-346 refuses unsupported names, duplicates, non-list selection and the credential name inside any serialized environment, invoked at preflight (core:1856) and dispatch (effects:975,1094,1211); supervisor env is PATH plus selected names only (ac_support_effects.py:1095,1108); presence booleans only (effects:1097,1213-1215; actor_cli.py:404); helper refuses HOME/CODEX_HOME overrides and non-Claude passthrough (actor_cli.py:137-142); policy digest rechecked before effects (effects:46-49, 446-449); receipts bound to requester and policy (effects:1049-1057). Tests: test_ac_support_environment_passthrough.py:36-40 and 96-106 use a fresh synthetic value and scan all retained files for leakage (lines 169-171); refusal controls at 188-218. B3: unsupported_* map to refused(capability) (ac_support_core.py:60); every observed operation_outcome carried limits \\\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\\\"; design fd-support-stdo-3.0.1.md:25-29 keeps timeout effect unknown; incomplete preserved through capture/check (test_ac_support_native301.py:76-97). B4: results.conjoin refused natively at ac_support_core.py:363-365 and 781-783, omitted from inventory (core:366) and listed unsupported (fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json:87-93; design:45-51); historical conjunction proof rejected by native return.check (test_ac_support_native301_conjunction.py:60-63); fd-stdo-3.0.1-binding.md:30-33 denies blanket F_D. B5: my own review.prepare calls wrote only protected evidence; the expectation artifact digest is identical in both phases; no candidate-tree write observed. B6: proof fixtures are controlled Python processes (test_ac_support_native301.py:80; passthrough test 96-106); the auth-repair-prep RETURN.json:23-24 test totals were not used as qualification. B7: examples README.md:109-126 and fd-support-stdo-3.0.1.md:53-76 describe the same policy/digest/principal CLI path I actually used.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"examples/fd-support/README.md:109-115,178-181; actor_cli.py:141-142; ac_support_effects.py:1232 together with actor_cli.py:386-387\",\"relation\":\"B2/B7 declared credential dependencies versus the claim that the adapter can invoke either host (fd-support-stdo-3.0.1.md:108-109)\",\"evidence\":\"Credential passthrough is Claude-only. The only path by which a Codex vendor process could find its login is HOME/CODEX_HOME placed in the registered executor environment (effects:1232) and re-read by the helper (actor_cli.py:386-387); no document declares that as the Codex credential route, and preflight does not evaluate it as one.\",\"consequence\":\"A nested Codex actor dispatched through this increment has no declared authentication contract. The increment does not claim one, so this is an open scope item, not a violated relation. Cause is demonstrated from code; whether it should be declared is the owner's call.\"},{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"repair-1/RETURN.json:74-78 versus candidate examples/fd-support/README.md (sha 53e2dbc3…, 12574 bytes)\",\"relation\":\"X1 reusable mechanical custody\",\"evidence\":\"The repair-1 proof source pins an earlier README (sha 0ada161f…, 11372 bytes); the current README bytes are covered only by the auth-repair-prep deliverable inventory, which is outside the claim population.\",\"consequence\":\"README custody for the passthrough section rests on a proof file I could not acquire; recorded as a residual, not a defect.\"}]},{\"id\":\"codex-tenant-static-merits\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"bound\":\"No actionable S0-S2 defect on the 12 inspected tenant files for static instruction and packaging paths; host discovery, Q01-Q12, efficiency, independent acceptance remain open as the claim itself states.\",\"evidence\":\"C1: DESIGN.md:5-9 binds the exact 3.0.1 manifest and common digests; DESIGN.md:15-28 maps SK-01..12 to algorithm, host/tool mechanism and finite proof; DESIGN.md:30 declares the codex-cli 0.164.0 execution binding; inventory.json:1-62 locates and freezes files and matches CODEX-CUSTODY.json:16 (whole population matches inventory plus self). C2: basis.md:13-27 declares its table as routes, not copied law; source-routes.json:4-7 and 99-106 carry method URI and native profile digest. C3: SKILL.md:12 direct Writer path without invented ticket or reviewer; SKILL.md:16 keeps availability, author assessment, independent review and acceptance separate; delegation.md:17 source-first reviewer, same-family limitation, no repair authorship; recovery.md:5-7 identical bytes with different histories; recovery.md:23 unperformed assessment has no result; no instruction to self-accept found. C4: tools.md:3 conjoin unsupported; tools.md:10-15 explicit policy, digest and principal; tools.md:17 process exit is not a verdict; the example SourceRef at tools.md:21 resolves to the acquired ACTIVATION.md 1004-1055 with matching digest. C5: SKILL.md:19 and DESIGN.md:13 acquire only the needed reference. C6: verify_package.py:78 states finite-bytes limits; README.md:13; qualification.md:7-18 keeps every Q case open. C7: README.md:3,50; DESIGN.md:3; CODEX-CUSTODY.json:3 \\\"no closed Worker return or semantic acceptance\\\".\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"references/recovery.md:17-23\",\"relation\":\"C2 routing not duplication (ACTIVATION §3 construction availability, acquired lines 1004-1055)\",\"evidence\":\"The construction-availability algebra is restated inside the skill without naming its owner clause in that paragraph; the restatement agrees with the acquired text (candidate_ready/satisfied, incomplete and refused/falsified, re_entry_requested cause to out_of_frame or invalid_basis).\",\"consequence\":\"Accurate under the immutable pin; drift risk only if the pin changes. Clarity item.\"},{\"severity\":\"S4\",\"location\":\"references/tools.md:5\",\"relation\":\"SK-11 resolvable references in delivered form (common WHAT, not oracle) and C4\",\"evidence\":\"A machine-specific absolute entrypoint path is written into the skill as construction provenance, with an instruction to re-resolve elsewhere.\",\"consequence\":\"Usable as provenance; a deployed copy depends on the operator resolving the tool path. Limited consequence.\"}]}],\"not_performed_within_components\":[\"Q01-Q12 host trials, automatic discovery, explicit invocation on a real Codex host\",\"execution of the shipped test suites (test code was inspected; the proof sources report runs)\",\"full line read of ac_support_core.py (3047 lines) and ac_support_effects.py (1365 lines)\",\"verification of codex/HOST.md (root successor) and the auth-repair-prep deliverable inventory, both outside the claim population\",\"efficiency, benefit, reliability and acceptance\"]},\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"sha256:9ed61889acb0caaec032092f45fbfa888ea63b6ae74b0be56d1301990c67bc4a\",\"sha256\":\"9ed61889acb0caaec032092f45fbfa888ea63b6ae74b0be56d1301990c67bc4a\"},{\"id\":\"sha256:6e10b4216d241c47c400c7a7186355018c2f4c1d8b64f8c1265e91882a7a2447\",\"sha256\":\"6e10b4216d241c47c400c7a7186355018c2f4c1d8b64f8c1265e91882a7a2447\"},{\"id\":\"sha256:ec9d5d5cc3709f9ddd6d3d9aff61dd8e5e70af48efbc8f62dafb6fb75613a2f1\",\"sha256\":\"ec9d5d5cc3709f9ddd6d3d9aff61dd8e5e70af48efbc8f62dafb6fb75613a2f1\"},{\"id\":\"sha256:d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\",\"sha256\":\"d152b7534fa985d91ea4304668ced42d7f3f914d2c6a04d730cdc86ea1308bcd\"},{\"id\":\"sha256:cdd9ae5b2b78e83285dd9ab22a0d09727bd24351a73c2bf1f0ca76f4f5e99157\",\"sha256\":\"cdd9ae5b2b78e83285dd9ab22a0d09727bd24351a73c2bf1f0ca76f4f5e99157\"},{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"USER-OUTCOME.md\",\"root\":\"review\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"008f733c9a6ee68e973ddebbaf71b8cb4106fd3f6b9af61a7e44c6d1c4579235\"},{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/EVALUATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[177,248]},\"sha256\":\"478fd21feda72d64e62a92f970b37bade3f9aadfb17c73649cdb1a7866581eff\"},{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standar